1
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:17,917
A makeover project
for your most unhinged leftovers.

2
00:00:17,984 --> 00:00:21,621
The best chefs in Korea will
turn your fridge inside out.

3
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,890
The classy cooking show has returned.

4
00:00:23,957 --> 00:00:27,560
<i>-Chef & My Fridge!</i>
<i>-My Fridge!</i>

5
00:00:28,261 --> 00:00:31,297
-Welcome.
-Welcome. It's great to see you all.

6
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:34,067
I see a few unfamiliar faces.

7
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:36,269
The studio is crowded today.

8
00:00:36,336 --> 00:00:37,437
It's too crowded.

9
00:00:37,504 --> 00:00:41,341
We actually prepared
a very special team round today.

10
00:00:41,574 --> 00:00:42,409
CURIOUS

11
00:00:42,475 --> 00:00:45,278
Instead of teaming up
two existing cast members,

12
00:00:45,345 --> 00:00:48,014
we've invited
two chefs' actual team members.

13
00:00:48,081 --> 00:00:50,116
The actual employees at their restaurants?

14
00:00:50,183 --> 00:00:52,452
We invited their right-hand men

15
00:00:52,519 --> 00:00:54,721
and put together a new kind of team round.

16
00:00:54,788 --> 00:00:56,222
-Sounds fun.
-We made it happen.

17
00:00:56,289 --> 00:00:58,591
It didn't happen suddenly, though.

18
00:00:58,658 --> 00:01:02,295
-So we planned it since last summer?
-Yes, you're right.

19
00:01:02,362 --> 00:01:06,032
Hyun-suk and I had a chance
to cook together,

20
00:01:06,099 --> 00:01:08,768
and during that event,
we thought it'd be fun

21
00:01:08,835 --> 00:01:12,172
to compete in these teams on the show.

22
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:13,106
And it happened.

23
00:01:13,173 --> 00:01:15,341
THE TEAM ROUND IS FINALLY HAPPENING

24
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:17,977
Hyun-suk's right-hand man,
can you tell us about yourself?

25
00:01:18,044 --> 00:01:19,479
Before he does that,

26
00:01:19,546 --> 00:01:21,848
let me blot out his nose first.

27
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:24,417
-Look how nice he is.
-How sweet.

28
00:01:24,484 --> 00:01:26,719
-He has to look good on the screen.
-Did he just flinch?

29
00:01:26,786 --> 00:01:28,755
-A little.
-I think he flinched a bit.

30
00:01:28,822 --> 00:01:30,824
He must've thought he was getting punched.

31
00:01:30,890 --> 00:01:31,724
Please say hello.

32
00:01:32,292 --> 00:01:35,929
Hello, I am head chef Kim Seon-yeop,

33
00:01:35,995 --> 00:01:38,531
who's been working
with Chef Hyun-suk for 14 years.

34
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:39,599
THE HEAD CHEF OF CHOI DOT

35
00:01:39,666 --> 00:01:41,901
How does it feel to be here?

36
00:01:41,968 --> 00:01:44,037
I can't believe I'm here,

37
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:47,707
the destination all chefs dream of.

38
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:49,576
-"The destination."
-This is the destination?

39
00:01:49,642 --> 00:01:51,845
Many young chefs dream
of being on <i>Chef & My Fridge.</i>

40
00:01:51,911 --> 00:01:53,313
So many.

41
00:01:53,379 --> 00:01:54,781
It was the destination for chefs?

42
00:01:54,848 --> 00:01:56,015
DREAMS COME TRUE

43
00:01:56,516 --> 00:01:59,219
I first met him as a student back in 2012.

44
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:00,386
How many years is that?

45
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:03,223
<i>And now, he feels like my other self,</i>
<i>someone I can't work without.</i>

46
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:04,591
<i>That's Chef Kim Seon-yeop.</i>

47
00:02:04,657 --> 00:02:06,593
If he's worked with you for 14 years,

48
00:02:06,659 --> 00:02:07,861
it already proves his character.

49
00:02:07,927 --> 00:02:10,029
-That's true.
-You must be one patient man.

50
00:02:10,096 --> 00:02:11,231
Such long years.

51
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:13,299
-How did he hold out?
-You're something.

52
00:02:13,366 --> 00:02:15,935
Once I retire, I wouldn't even mind
passing my position to him.

53
00:02:16,002 --> 00:02:17,537
Really?

54
00:02:17,604 --> 00:02:20,874
-Step down!
-Step down!

55
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:22,509
-Step down!
-Step down, Hyun-suk!

56
00:02:22,575 --> 00:02:23,610
Can you punch him once?

57
00:02:23,843 --> 00:02:25,211
NEEDS HIS RIGHT-HAND MAN'S HELP

58
00:02:25,278 --> 00:02:28,047
Why don't we meet
Chef Jong-won's right-hand man too?

59
00:02:28,114 --> 00:02:31,151
-He's also good-looking.
-Isn't he?

60
00:02:31,217 --> 00:02:33,019
Doesn't he remind you
of Jung Hyuk, the model?

61
00:02:33,086 --> 00:02:36,523
THE RESEMBLANCE IS THERE

62
00:02:36,589 --> 00:02:38,625
Why don't you say hello too?

63
00:02:38,691 --> 00:02:39,726
Hello.

64
00:02:39,792 --> 00:02:42,162
I am Woo Do-hee,
and I work at L'Amant Secret.

65
00:02:42,228 --> 00:02:45,832
I've always enjoyed this show
since my days as a military cook.

66
00:02:45,899 --> 00:02:48,134
-You were a mess cook?
-Yes, I was.

67
00:02:48,201 --> 00:02:49,502
He was a mess cook too.

68
00:02:49,569 --> 00:02:50,537
Great to meet you.

69
00:02:50,603 --> 00:02:52,405
A BIG SMILE TO SHOW HIS GLADNESS

70
00:02:52,472 --> 00:02:55,208
-I don't know why, but I like him.
-A military cook.

71
00:02:55,275 --> 00:02:56,910
Tell us about him, Jong-won.

72
00:02:56,976 --> 00:03:00,480
<i>He's been working with me</i>
<i>for three years now.</i>

73
00:03:00,547 --> 00:03:02,916
He's someone who makes up
for the things I lack.

74
00:03:02,982 --> 00:03:06,753
-I always know that he has my back.
-So you can trust him.

75
00:03:06,819 --> 00:03:09,522
Jong-won, do you only hire
those who have a similar hairstyle?

76
00:03:10,823 --> 00:03:13,293
-I don't care about looks, but hair, yes.
-The hair.

77
00:03:13,593 --> 00:03:14,961
ONE CONDITION: GOOD HAIR VIBES

78
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:16,863
Chef Do-hee is nicknamed

79
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:18,131
Dupe Jong-won.

80
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:19,532
-Dupe Jong-won?
-Dupe Jong-won?

81
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:21,234
-Dupe Jong-won?
-What's this about?

82
00:03:21,301 --> 00:03:24,370
Well, the lighting is rather low
at our restaurant,

83
00:03:24,437 --> 00:03:25,872
and our silhouettes are similar,

84
00:03:25,939 --> 00:03:28,374
so some guests take me for him.

85
00:03:28,441 --> 00:03:30,610
They have similar builds.
So are their silhouettes.

86
00:03:30,677 --> 00:03:33,680
-People must go, "Jong-won is here."
-"He's here."

87
00:03:33,746 --> 00:03:35,415
At first, they whisper,

88
00:03:35,481 --> 00:03:37,517
then they look disappointed
when I approach.

89
00:03:37,784 --> 00:03:39,586
SORRY TO DISAPPOINT

90
00:03:39,652 --> 00:03:40,954
So people at L'Amant Secret

91
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:44,490
call him Chef de Disappointment.

92
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:47,126
-It's supposed to be "cuisine."
-Not chef de cuisine.

93
00:03:47,193 --> 00:03:49,562
He has a great physique, doesn't he?

94
00:03:49,629 --> 00:03:53,233
So some call him Wide-Shouldered, WS.

95
00:03:53,299 --> 00:03:55,702
You're right. Look at his biceps.

96
00:03:55,768 --> 00:03:57,170
When it comes to shoulders,

97
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:59,806
-this guy's even bigger than Ma Dong-seok.
-Right.

98
00:03:59,872 --> 00:04:02,408
-He has
-Ma Dong-seok of the culinary world.

99
00:04:02,475 --> 00:04:04,310
-the craziest back.
-Yes, you're right.

100
00:04:04,377 --> 00:04:06,613
-He's no joke, right? Hey, Poong.
-Really.

101
00:04:06,679 --> 00:04:09,015
You'll end up in diapers
once he punches you with these.

102
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:11,017
-I get it.
-Don't get smart with me.

103
00:04:11,284 --> 00:04:12,518
FEELING CONFIDENT WITH A SIDEKICK

104
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:14,420
Actually, I was a bit worried.

105
00:04:14,487 --> 00:04:17,724
After all, <i>Chef & My Fridge</i>
is a show that is meant to entertain,

106
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:19,692
but this guy has too much respect for me.

107
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:22,095
He jokes around a lot
and is funny when he's alone,

108
00:04:22,161 --> 00:04:24,397
but with me,
he only shows respect, respect, respect.

109
00:04:24,464 --> 00:04:27,133
So I told our scriptwriter
we'd give up on entertaining

110
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,868
and only focus on cooking this time

111
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:30,870
-because he's with me.
-He won't let him talk.

112
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:32,338
Can you step outside for a moment then?

113
00:04:34,007 --> 00:04:36,376
We want to have
a fun chat with Chef Seon-yeop.

114
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:38,011
We get that you respect him,

115
00:04:38,077 --> 00:04:41,714
but what if you had to single out
one weakness that he has?

116
00:04:41,914 --> 00:04:42,915
HESITANT

117
00:04:42,982 --> 00:04:44,183
He tends to…

118
00:04:44,250 --> 00:04:46,219
SEON-YEOP!

119
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:48,154
He tends to fish for praise.

120
00:04:48,221 --> 00:04:49,989
Whoa. He fishes for compliments.

121
00:04:50,056 --> 00:04:52,525
-He tends to do that.
-He talks perfectly well.

122
00:04:52,592 --> 00:04:54,294
-What do you mean, only respect?
-He's good.

123
00:04:54,594 --> 00:04:56,396
UNCOVERING THE TRUTH WITH A KIND SMILE

124
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:58,431
What specific thing did I do
to fish for praise?

125
00:04:58,698 --> 00:04:59,666
THE WORST QUESTION

126
00:04:59,732 --> 00:05:01,000
He doesn't know what he did.

127
00:05:01,067 --> 00:05:03,936
Thanks to me,
he got to travel around the world.

128
00:05:04,604 --> 00:05:06,406
He must've dreaded it so much.

129
00:05:06,739 --> 00:05:07,907
CATHARTIC

130
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:09,375
He absolutely does fish for it.

131
00:05:09,442 --> 00:05:11,277
PRAISE FISHER CHOI

132
00:05:11,344 --> 00:05:15,615
I've watched them
in the kitchen as a third party,

133
00:05:15,682 --> 00:05:17,250
and Chef Seon-yeop

134
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:20,053
once let out the biggest sigh
from the bottom of his heart and said,

135
00:05:20,119 --> 00:05:23,489
"I should do it."
He said it with such a deep sigh.

136
00:05:23,556 --> 00:05:25,558
-"I should do it."
-"I should do it."

137
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:28,394
-I've seen him let out that deep sigh.
-He has a lot to tell.

138
00:05:28,461 --> 00:05:30,830
When our production crew
called him for a pre-interview,

139
00:05:30,897 --> 00:05:32,465
he would not hang up.

140
00:05:32,532 --> 00:05:33,933
Gosh, it usually isn't that long.

141
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,368
He had things he wanted to share.

142
00:05:35,435 --> 00:05:38,538
-We have the transcript of the call.
-We do?

143
00:05:38,604 --> 00:05:40,006
Chef Seon-yeop said,

144
00:05:40,573 --> 00:05:43,009
"I'll probably end up
only cleaning up his mess."

145
00:05:44,944 --> 00:05:46,913
That means that's what he always does!

146
00:05:46,979 --> 00:05:49,015
How should we perceive this?

147
00:05:49,082 --> 00:05:51,718
When he cooks,

148
00:05:53,086 --> 00:05:54,354
he tends to make a mess.

149
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:56,222
AN EXPERT AT MAKING A MESS

150
00:05:56,289 --> 00:05:59,092
-Unlike Chef Jong-won, who always wipes.
-He does.

151
00:05:59,158 --> 00:06:01,194
SUDDENLY STOPS TALKING…

152
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:03,296
Fifteen minutes are already fairly short,

153
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:05,732
so I thought I'd end up
only cleaning up after him.

154
00:06:06,899 --> 00:06:09,335
Things weren't too different on this side.

155
00:06:09,402 --> 00:06:11,604
-What?
-He also spent

156
00:06:11,671 --> 00:06:14,574
-all night on the phone with our crew.
-Are you serious?

157
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,275
What did he have to say?

158
00:06:16,342 --> 00:06:17,677
He's scary.

159
00:06:17,744 --> 00:06:21,447
He said, "I'm often surprised
while watching <i>Chef & My Fridge.</i>"

160
00:06:21,514 --> 00:06:24,751
"He often flies off the handle
when he's with us,

161
00:06:24,817 --> 00:06:27,720
so it's really strange
to see him seem so shy on the show."

162
00:06:27,787 --> 00:06:30,256
He must feel like a stranger!

163
00:06:30,323 --> 00:06:32,859
How should we take this?
How is he different?

164
00:06:32,925 --> 00:06:34,227
-Is he mad?
-I think

165
00:06:34,293 --> 00:06:37,630
-he's a tough guy in the kitchen.
-A tough guy.

166
00:06:37,697 --> 00:06:41,401
It's a rare sight
to see him seem shy at work,

167
00:06:41,467 --> 00:06:43,569
-so it's strange.
-So he's not like that at all?

168
00:06:43,636 --> 00:06:45,905
Last time, he did the strikeout thing.

169
00:06:45,972 --> 00:06:47,273
<i>Did you watch that episode?</i>

170
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:48,941
-Yes, the strikeout pose.
-I did.

171
00:06:49,008 --> 00:06:50,510
I got

172
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:54,147
-secondhand embarrassment watching him.
-Yes, I'm sure.

173
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:57,350
CRINGED HARD
WHILE WATCHING HIS BOSS AT WORK

174
00:06:57,417 --> 00:07:00,953
-Jong-won looks flushed.
-He doesn't know what to do.

175
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:02,288
It's an emergency.

176
00:07:02,355 --> 00:07:03,489
I think it's my job

177
00:07:03,556 --> 00:07:06,793
to entertain people
when I'm shooting the show.

178
00:07:06,859 --> 00:07:09,328
-I've been doing my best.
-Yes, you're trying.

179
00:07:09,395 --> 00:07:12,064
Chef Do-hee feels
secondhand embarrassment, right?

180
00:07:12,131 --> 00:07:13,900
This guy says

181
00:07:13,966 --> 00:07:17,537
he always feels secondhand pride

182
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:19,138
-through me.
-Secondhand pride.

183
00:07:19,205 --> 00:07:21,808
Why do you
keep saying these things yourself?

184
00:07:21,874 --> 00:07:23,075
Stop it!

185
00:07:23,142 --> 00:07:25,578
-He just sighed.
-See? I told you so.

186
00:07:25,645 --> 00:07:28,714
-That was such a loud sigh.
-You tell them. You can relax and talk.

187
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:31,684
He can't seem to relax,
so how is he supposed to do that?

188
00:07:31,751 --> 00:07:33,219
Will you just let him talk?

189
00:07:33,486 --> 00:07:34,854
HAS LOTS TO SAY BUT WON'T

190
00:07:34,921 --> 00:07:37,056
I'm looking forward to today.

191
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:39,425
-We don't know what the order is.
-But they will compete.

192
00:07:39,492 --> 00:07:41,060
Yes, that's decided.

193
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:44,964
-Let's invite today's guests now.
-The guests.

194
00:07:45,031 --> 00:07:48,301
They're people that we all hoped
would come and dine with us,

195
00:07:48,367 --> 00:07:52,538
and they found time to join us today
despite their busy schedule.

196
00:07:52,605 --> 00:07:55,741
Please welcome today's fridge owners!

197
00:07:55,808 --> 00:07:57,276
Come on out!

198
00:07:58,911 --> 00:08:00,713
Today's fridge owners.

199
00:08:01,514 --> 00:08:03,549
Welcome!

200
00:08:03,616 --> 00:08:06,886
-KARINA and WINTER of aespa!
-It's great to see you!

201
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:08,721
STANDING OVATION

202
00:08:08,788 --> 00:08:09,889
-I'm blushing.
-Please welcome

203
00:08:09,956 --> 00:08:12,158
KARINA and WINTER of aespa!
Welcome to the show!

204
00:08:12,391 --> 00:08:13,759
WELCOME

205
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:15,061
WELCOMING PASSIONATELY

206
00:08:15,127 --> 00:08:16,429
Oh, man.

207
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,231
I can't believe
I'm meeting you two in person.

208
00:08:18,297 --> 00:08:19,699
Let us greet you. Two, three.

209
00:08:19,765 --> 00:08:22,201
-Hello, we're aespa.
-Hello, we're aespa.

210
00:08:22,268 --> 00:08:24,003
Oh, man.

211
00:08:24,070 --> 00:08:25,805
Will you stop saying that?

212
00:08:26,472 --> 00:08:28,474
How many times do you have to say that?

213
00:08:29,408 --> 00:08:31,511
Oh, man. Seriously.

214
00:08:35,781 --> 00:08:37,383
I have K-pop idol experts at home,

215
00:08:37,450 --> 00:08:40,620
so I was already educated.

216
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:44,190
Why don't you meet the new chefs
and say hello to them too?

217
00:08:44,257 --> 00:08:45,658
-Right.
-Hello.

218
00:08:45,992 --> 00:08:47,660
SAYING HI TO THE OTHER SIDE

219
00:08:48,728 --> 00:08:50,763
Their faces lit up instantly.

220
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:52,231
HAPPY

221
00:08:52,298 --> 00:08:53,866
SLAPPING THE RIGHT-HAND MAN

222
00:08:53,933 --> 00:08:54,967
Seon-yeop!

223
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,802
I should prick your ears
to make them less red.

224
00:08:58,037 --> 00:09:00,039
-He's so red.
-He's blushing more and more.

225
00:09:00,106 --> 00:09:05,311
I got to check how many teeth you have.
You have great teeth.

226
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:09,282
I heard that you two
really love <i>Chef & My Fridge.</i>

227
00:09:09,348 --> 00:09:12,084
-We're huge fans.
-You are?

228
00:09:12,151 --> 00:09:14,053
And now that I'm actually here,

229
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:15,154
it feels so cool.

230
00:09:15,488 --> 00:09:16,989
GIGGLE

231
00:09:17,056 --> 00:09:19,625
And the same for us.
We find it so cool too.

232
00:09:19,692 --> 00:09:20,927
WINTER, you've watched us

233
00:09:20,993 --> 00:09:23,462
-since your early teens?
-You did?

234
00:09:23,529 --> 00:09:26,232
Yes, it must've been 2014.

235
00:09:26,299 --> 00:09:28,668
-I was in middle school.
-We started back then.

236
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:30,836
I'd watch it over a meal with my mom.

237
00:09:31,704 --> 00:09:34,941
I remember us both getting mesmerized
at how the chefs cooked.

238
00:09:35,007 --> 00:09:37,043
-And that teen grew up to be here.
-Right?

239
00:09:37,109 --> 00:09:38,210
NOW SHE'S ON THE SHOW

240
00:09:38,277 --> 00:09:41,013
-That's true.
-Anyway, KARINA.

241
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,616
-I heard you came very determined.
-Is that so?

242
00:09:43,683 --> 00:09:44,517
Yes, I plan

243
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,252
to go very far today.

244
00:09:46,319 --> 00:09:48,521
-You plan to go very far?
-Why would a guest do that?

245
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:50,990
I really enjoyed Ye-eun's episode

246
00:09:51,057 --> 00:09:54,226
as well as Yu-jin's episode.

247
00:09:54,293 --> 00:09:56,095
I hope our episodes are the funniest.

248
00:09:56,529 --> 00:09:57,363
THAT'S AESPA'S SPIRIT

249
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:58,931
I knew it.

250
00:09:58,998 --> 00:10:01,901
-We're here to be funny for you!
-Yes.

251
00:10:01,968 --> 00:10:06,305
We can make it funny. We'll do it.

252
00:10:07,473 --> 00:10:08,741
WOW…

253
00:10:08,808 --> 00:10:11,944
What if I asked you to come with me
for the five-minute check?

254
00:10:12,011 --> 00:10:13,112
If you'd like, of course.

255
00:10:13,179 --> 00:10:15,348
-I'm ready for it.
-Are you?

256
00:10:15,414 --> 00:10:16,682
-You're in?
-Yes.

257
00:10:16,749 --> 00:10:19,552
-And WINTER? Great.
-I'm ready too.

258
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,754
I heard KARINA prepared
a party trick for us.

259
00:10:21,821 --> 00:10:23,556
You prepared a party trick?

260
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,091
-She's prepared.
-It's not that.

261
00:10:25,157 --> 00:10:27,426
-This is big.
-Really?

262
00:10:27,493 --> 00:10:28,661
Can we see it?

263
00:10:30,262 --> 00:10:32,965
I'm sure you had been busy
promoting your new album.

264
00:10:33,032 --> 00:10:34,800
-So?
-Well, it's…

265
00:10:34,867 --> 00:10:37,903
We often say
people clap like fur seals, right?

266
00:10:37,970 --> 00:10:40,006
So I came up with the seal clap.

267
00:10:40,072 --> 00:10:41,507
-The seal clap?
-The seal clap?

268
00:10:41,574 --> 00:10:43,309
CHUCKLE…

269
00:10:43,376 --> 00:10:44,477
Is it already funny?

270
00:10:44,543 --> 00:10:45,811
SO MUCH PRESSURE

271
00:10:46,379 --> 00:10:48,614
-I think it'll be really funny.
-Don't expect too much.

272
00:10:48,681 --> 00:10:50,716
But please laugh out loud for me.

273
00:10:50,783 --> 00:10:52,251
-Yes, of course.
-No worries!

274
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,787
EVERYONE BEGINS TO LAUGH

275
00:10:54,854 --> 00:10:56,522
I'm ready to die from laughing.

276
00:10:56,856 --> 00:10:58,057
MOVED

277
00:10:58,124 --> 00:11:00,426
Okay. I'll do it.

278
00:11:00,926 --> 00:11:01,761
CHUCKLE

279
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:03,362
LAUNCH THE SEAL CLAP

280
00:11:03,963 --> 00:11:05,264
LAUNCH THE REACTION

281
00:11:06,932 --> 00:11:08,567
I'M SO GRATEFUL FOR HIM…

282
00:11:08,768 --> 00:11:11,871
GOOD ONE

283
00:11:11,937 --> 00:11:13,539
That was funny.

284
00:11:13,606 --> 00:11:15,141
THE ADDICTIVE SEAL CLAP

285
00:11:15,207 --> 00:11:17,777
-I'm feeling hot now.
-Thanks for that.

286
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:20,146
Actually, there's an actual seal
on our show.

287
00:11:20,212 --> 00:11:21,647
Is there a seal among us?

288
00:11:21,714 --> 00:11:23,516
Ho-young's pretty much an actual seal.

289
00:11:23,582 --> 00:11:25,051
Can you do this for us?

290
00:11:25,284 --> 00:11:26,886
JUST LIKE A SEAL

291
00:11:26,952 --> 00:11:28,487
He can do it right away.

292
00:11:28,554 --> 00:11:30,723
You can't steal it from me.

293
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:32,324
Do you have anything, WINTER?

294
00:11:32,558 --> 00:11:33,392
WONDERING…

295
00:11:33,459 --> 00:11:35,227
Yes! I can…

296
00:11:35,294 --> 00:11:37,196
I just thought of something.

297
00:11:37,263 --> 00:11:38,597
I can rotate my hand 360 degrees.

298
00:11:38,898 --> 00:11:40,166
360 DEGREES?

299
00:11:40,232 --> 00:11:41,400
-Your hand?
-Hand?

300
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:42,768
-Her hand?
-Let me show you.

301
00:11:42,835 --> 00:11:43,903
Rotate it all the way?

302
00:11:43,969 --> 00:11:45,404
-Most people can do this, right?
-Yes.

303
00:11:45,905 --> 00:11:46,972
I can flip it again.

304
00:11:49,742 --> 00:11:51,043
I CAN EVEN ROTATE IT TOO

305
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:54,080
-What?
-What was that?

306
00:11:54,146 --> 00:11:55,715
Wait a minute. How flexible are you?

307
00:11:55,781 --> 00:11:57,483
-How did she do that?
-I just can.

308
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:59,185
HOW DID SHE DO THAT?

309
00:11:59,585 --> 00:12:00,686
LIKE THIS?

310
00:12:00,753 --> 00:12:02,388
How does she flip it this way?

311
00:12:02,455 --> 00:12:04,256
OUCH…

312
00:12:04,323 --> 00:12:07,159
-You have to cook later.
-Please be careful.

313
00:12:08,027 --> 00:12:10,529
That's why she could
do this dance so naturally.

314
00:12:10,596 --> 00:12:13,032
That could be a surprising party trick.

315
00:12:13,099 --> 00:12:14,500
-Good start.
-Off to a great start.

316
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:15,935
WE GOT THIS

317
00:12:16,001 --> 00:12:18,337
Also, I hear WINTER

318
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:20,606
has a teacher among the chefs.

319
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:22,808
-Hey.
-Really?

320
00:12:22,875 --> 00:12:25,411
-Did I?
-"Did I?"

321
00:12:25,478 --> 00:12:28,647
It might be true or not. So who is it?

322
00:12:28,714 --> 00:12:32,752
-Chef Sung-jun is my teacher, actually.
-What?

323
00:12:32,818 --> 00:12:35,154
-He is? Sung-jun?
-Yes.

324
00:12:35,221 --> 00:12:37,389
Don't open your eyes like that. Please.

325
00:12:37,456 --> 00:12:39,525
What did you possibly learn from him?

326
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:44,530
A while back, Sung-jun said
he'd send me pistachio cream.

327
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:46,632
He said he'd send it to me.

328
00:12:46,699 --> 00:12:49,168
-But he never did.
-Come on.

329
00:12:49,235 --> 00:12:50,503
-He didn't?
-Why didn't you?

330
00:12:50,569 --> 00:12:51,537
Boo.

331
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:52,872
But I didn't have your address.

332
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:54,807
-You could've sent it to her agency.
-Her agency.

333
00:12:54,874 --> 00:12:56,075
-To her agency?
-Yes.

334
00:12:56,142 --> 00:12:57,309
Right-o.

335
00:12:57,710 --> 00:12:59,879
SUNG-JUN DE DISAPPOINTMENT…

336
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:02,181
On top of that, I wasn't his best student.

337
00:13:02,248 --> 00:13:04,049
-He has someone else?
-Yes.

338
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:06,719
He outright told me I was second place.

339
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:09,155
-She'd mostly be everyone's first.
-Right?

340
00:13:09,221 --> 00:13:11,023
Did you have to say that?

341
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:12,458
-That's the worst.
-Actually,

342
00:13:12,525 --> 00:13:15,394
I do have one student I cherish,
someone who is very good at cooking.

343
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:18,330
I also wish we could have him here,
someone named Faker.

344
00:13:18,397 --> 00:13:20,699
-Just be second place.
-Yes, the professional gamer.

345
00:13:20,766 --> 00:13:23,202
-Quiet.
-He's an excellent cook.

346
00:13:23,269 --> 00:13:25,337
Is he really?

347
00:13:26,105 --> 00:13:29,542
So I'm here to look for a new teacher.

348
00:13:29,608 --> 00:13:30,442
GREAT NEWS

349
00:13:30,509 --> 00:13:32,478
-A new chef?
-Do that.

350
00:13:32,545 --> 00:13:34,246
Just find someone new.

351
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:36,415
Sung-jun isn't the only chef
you can learn from.

352
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:38,918
-Right, everyone here can be a teacher.
-Emergency.

353
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:41,287
Her teacher is always
looking for a new teacher too.

354
00:13:41,353 --> 00:13:43,088
-You're right.
-Yes.

355
00:13:43,155 --> 00:13:45,357
-Like teacher, like student.
-Emergency.

356
00:13:45,424 --> 00:13:48,627
-I'll find a new teacher today.
-See if you want anyone else.

357
00:13:48,694 --> 00:13:50,963
Is there anyone you're considering?

358
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:52,231
I considered

359
00:13:52,298 --> 00:13:54,733
Chef Hyun-suk or…

360
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,068
He's on her radar.

361
00:13:56,135 --> 00:13:58,504
-Right hand down, please.
-Yes, please.

362
00:13:58,971 --> 00:13:59,905
HEHE

363
00:13:59,972 --> 00:14:01,974
-Or Chef Sam.
-Sam.

364
00:14:02,041 --> 00:14:05,044
-Why did you skip me just like that?
-No!

365
00:14:05,110 --> 00:14:06,478
Poong was right in the middle.

366
00:14:06,545 --> 00:14:09,481
-He's right there, but she skipped him.
-I was even looking at her.

367
00:14:09,548 --> 00:14:10,916
You just aren't it.

368
00:14:10,983 --> 00:14:14,153
-I'm sure WINTER will find…
-Of course.

369
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:17,089
…her new teacher after today's cook-offs.

370
00:14:17,156 --> 00:14:20,192
aespa is from the famous agency,
SM Entertainment,

371
00:14:20,259 --> 00:14:22,394
-and they are their flagship group.
-Yes.

372
00:14:22,461 --> 00:14:23,662
WE'RE THE FLAGSHIP GROUP?

373
00:14:23,729 --> 00:14:27,733
And these two are known to have
the textbook SM Entertainment look.

374
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,301
-They do.
-I think WINTER

375
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:31,136
was definitely born to be in SM.

376
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:32,538
-WINTER more than you?
-Yes.

377
00:14:32,605 --> 00:14:35,674
She reminds me
of both Seo Hyun-jin and Taeyeon,

378
00:14:35,741 --> 00:14:37,977
all very fair and…

379
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:39,778
They always include a member like that.

380
00:14:39,845 --> 00:14:42,548
-I think it applies more to KARINA.
-Yes?

381
00:14:42,615 --> 00:14:44,149
-Rather?
-It's like we're at a pageant.

382
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,719
-So KARINA has the textbook SM look?
-Yes, I think so.

383
00:14:46,785 --> 00:14:50,356
I actually didn't make the cut
for the audition like three times.

384
00:14:50,422 --> 00:14:54,193
I kept auditioning again and again
until I got in.

385
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:58,497
But in her case,
the agency contacted her first, via DM.

386
00:14:58,564 --> 00:15:00,733
She was chosen by them,

387
00:15:00,799 --> 00:15:03,402
whereas I chose the agency.

388
00:15:03,469 --> 00:15:06,839
-So that's how people are cast now?
-They do that these days.

389
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:09,141
-Back in my day, it was on the streets.
-The streets.

390
00:15:09,208 --> 00:15:11,143
People were cast on the streets.

391
00:15:11,210 --> 00:15:12,745
-At Bupyeong Station or…
-Gangnam Station.

392
00:15:12,811 --> 00:15:14,179
-Bupyeong Station?
-Bupyeong.

393
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,348
-Street dancers lurked there.
-You hung out at Bupyeong?

394
00:15:16,415 --> 00:15:19,151
Lots of street dancers were there,
so they'd get picked up.

395
00:15:19,218 --> 00:15:21,320
That's how people were picked up.

396
00:15:21,387 --> 00:15:24,957
Wait a second.
I have a surprising transcript.

397
00:15:25,024 --> 00:15:27,459
WINTER said one of the chefs

398
00:15:27,526 --> 00:15:30,396
-had the typical SM Entertainment look.
-There is?

399
00:15:30,462 --> 00:15:33,465
-One of you has that look.
-The SM Entertainment look?

400
00:15:33,532 --> 00:15:34,667
Could it be Eun-yeong?

401
00:15:34,733 --> 00:15:36,735
She looks quite hopeful.

402
00:15:36,802 --> 00:15:38,003
GIGGLE

403
00:15:38,070 --> 00:15:40,172
-Right. Cut it out.
-No way.

404
00:15:40,239 --> 00:15:42,241
It's a great agency for idol stars.

405
00:15:42,308 --> 00:15:43,809
-No way.
-SM Entertainment sounds right.

406
00:15:43,876 --> 00:15:44,977
So who has that look?

407
00:15:45,044 --> 00:15:47,546
First, Chef Jong-won.

408
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:48,914
TYPICAL SM ENTERTAINMENT LOOK

409
00:15:48,981 --> 00:15:50,349
-I can see it.
-Anyone else?

410
00:15:51,050 --> 00:15:52,952
Chef Ho-young.

411
00:15:53,018 --> 00:15:54,486
-Ho-young?
-What?

412
00:15:55,354 --> 00:15:56,555
Ho-young?

413
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:58,257
-I can't agree.
-Are you saying this

414
00:15:58,324 --> 00:16:00,292
-just to flatter him? Really?
-I'm serious.

415
00:16:00,359 --> 00:16:02,761
There's always that one member
called the fan magnet.

416
00:16:02,828 --> 00:16:04,763
-"Fan magnet"?
-Right.

417
00:16:04,830 --> 00:16:06,799
-What's a fan magnet?
-That's a thing.

418
00:16:06,865 --> 00:16:08,067
Is that a good thing?

419
00:16:08,133 --> 00:16:09,401
-It is.
-It is?

420
00:16:09,468 --> 00:16:11,136
-He has that look.
-There's that niche.

421
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:12,638
IF IT'S A GOOD THING, OKAY THEN

422
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:16,175
DEFINITELY THE FAN MAGNET

423
00:16:16,241 --> 00:16:19,812
You two brought two separate fridges.

424
00:16:19,878 --> 00:16:21,080
Do you live separately?

425
00:16:21,146 --> 00:16:22,548
That's not the case.

426
00:16:22,614 --> 00:16:25,017
We actually had two dorms
for two members each

427
00:16:25,084 --> 00:16:27,453
but recently moved into one place.

428
00:16:27,519 --> 00:16:32,191
We brought both fridges
from our previous places,

429
00:16:32,257 --> 00:16:33,659
so we ended up with two.

430
00:16:33,726 --> 00:16:36,929
They live in the same dorm,
but they use different fridges.

431
00:16:36,996 --> 00:16:37,963
-Shall we?
-Let's go.

432
00:16:38,030 --> 00:16:40,532
Let's go through WINTER's fridge.

433
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:43,302
I literally have nothing.

434
00:16:43,369 --> 00:16:47,072
-You don't?
-All I kept in there were beverages

435
00:16:47,139 --> 00:16:49,108
because I had no time to eat
back at the dorm.

436
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:52,311
But I recently started
to aim for a healthier lifestyle,

437
00:16:52,378 --> 00:16:54,480
so I've been slowly filling it up.

438
00:16:54,546 --> 00:16:55,781
I still might not have much.

439
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:57,549
We haven't even opened it.

440
00:16:57,616 --> 00:16:58,951
-I feel so…
-Excuses.

441
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:01,553
-I feel anxious.
-Do you?

442
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:03,789
Wait, as you can see,

443
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:06,225
the shelf-stable ingredients
are all right in the middle.

444
00:17:06,291 --> 00:17:09,828
Do you share these ingredients?

445
00:17:09,895 --> 00:17:11,397
-Do you share these?
-We just

446
00:17:11,463 --> 00:17:13,599
steal each other's food
whenever the other isn't looking.

447
00:17:13,832 --> 00:17:16,235
AS STEALTHY AS THEIR CHOREOGRAPHY

448
00:17:16,301 --> 00:17:18,404
-What's this?
-A <i>ramyeon </i>cooker.

449
00:17:18,470 --> 00:17:20,639
-It's mine.
-KARINA's?

450
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:22,508
It's the famous
Hangang River <i>ramyeon</i> cooker.

451
00:17:22,574 --> 00:17:24,843
My friend gave it to me
as a birthday present.

452
00:17:24,910 --> 00:17:27,613
-Because you love <i>ramyeon?</i>
-Shows my power, doesn't it?

453
00:17:27,679 --> 00:17:29,014
I love it so much.

454
00:17:29,081 --> 00:17:31,517
So are these all yours?

455
00:17:31,583 --> 00:17:35,020
Actually, among these
shelf-stable ingredients,

456
00:17:35,087 --> 00:17:38,123
mine are just the cooker and alcohol.
Everything else is WINTER's.

457
00:17:38,190 --> 00:17:40,492
-Everything else belongs to WINTER?
-That's right.

458
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:42,227
Do you see that scale?

459
00:17:42,294 --> 00:17:44,196
-This one?
-That means someone in that house…

460
00:17:44,263 --> 00:17:46,331
-You're right.
-…is an avid cook.

461
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:47,933
I'm sorry, but it's for body weight.

462
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:50,536
A JOKE JUST FOR GIRL GROUPS

463
00:17:50,602 --> 00:17:52,938
-I guess they can do that.
-They're that light.

464
00:17:53,005 --> 00:17:55,040
Right. For them?

465
00:17:55,107 --> 00:17:57,743
-It's mine.
-Was she into baking?

466
00:17:57,810 --> 00:17:59,878
I wanted to make Dubai chewy cookies

467
00:17:59,945 --> 00:18:03,982
-and heard measuring is very important.
-You're right.

468
00:18:04,049 --> 00:18:06,018
I'm always trying to cook.

469
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:08,253
Then for this episode and the next,

470
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:11,857
will WINTER only use her ingredients,
and KARINA only hers?

471
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:14,493
-We'll use them together.
-It sounds unfair, though.

472
00:18:14,726 --> 00:18:17,629
AESPA IS ONE, WE CAN'T BE TWO

473
00:18:17,696 --> 00:18:19,531
-Thank you!
-Right?

474
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:22,634
-It feels unfair.
-You can see truffle oil and stuff here.

475
00:18:22,701 --> 00:18:27,039
-We present aespa WINTER's fridge!
-Fridge!

476
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,307
-Fridge!
-Fridge!

477
00:18:29,374 --> 00:18:31,777
LUKEWARM RESPONSE

478
00:18:32,044 --> 00:18:34,179
EMBARRASSED

479
00:18:34,446 --> 00:18:37,149
PRESENTING WINTER'S FRIDGE

480
00:18:37,749 --> 00:18:40,819
-There is some stuff.
-She has a few things.

481
00:18:40,886 --> 00:18:43,822
I thought you'd only have beverages,
so this isn't too bad.

482
00:18:43,889 --> 00:18:45,757
Yes, you have quite a lot.

483
00:18:45,824 --> 00:18:47,059
She doesn't have too much,

484
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,694
but she put them on display nicely.

485
00:18:49,261 --> 00:18:53,165
-She made it look fuller.
-She could've put it all on one shelf.

486
00:18:53,232 --> 00:18:54,933
She spread it all out.

487
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,768
The second shelf has…

488
00:18:56,835 --> 00:18:59,138
-Some side dishes.
-Korean <i>banchan</i>.

489
00:18:59,204 --> 00:19:01,540
My mom made and sent them to me.

490
00:19:01,607 --> 00:19:03,642
Delicious side dishes.

491
00:19:03,709 --> 00:19:04,710
Where's your hometown?

492
00:19:04,776 --> 00:19:05,911
-Yangsan.
-Yangsan.

493
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:08,046
-With Tongdosa Temple.
-Yes, Tongdosa Temple.

494
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:10,449
KNOWN FOR TONGDOSA TEMPLE

495
00:19:10,516 --> 00:19:12,417
-The same word for sun umbrella.
-Right.

496
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:14,987
HA HA HA HA

497
00:19:15,287 --> 00:19:17,289
ALSO GOING, HA HA HA

498
00:19:17,356 --> 00:19:19,591
Was it that bad?

499
00:19:19,658 --> 00:19:22,761
-He must be under so much pressure.
-That was so tacky.

500
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:24,263
<i>-Makjang!</i>
<i>-Makjang?</i>

501
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:25,898
<i>-Makjang?</i>
-Is this your mom's writing?

502
00:19:25,964 --> 00:19:27,966
-Yes, to prevent confusion.
-She labeled it.

503
00:19:28,033 --> 00:19:31,503
-It's so good with chili pepper.
-Yes, or <i>sundae</i>, Korean sausage.

504
00:19:31,570 --> 00:19:34,006
I ordered <i>sundae</i> in Seoul,
and it only came with salt.

505
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:36,241
WINTER IS MORE USED
TO EATING IT WITH MAKJANG

506
00:19:36,308 --> 00:19:38,277
<i>I need </i>makjang<i> with it.</i>

507
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:40,512
Just as <i>mandu</i>, dumplings,
come with soy sauce,

508
00:19:40,579 --> 00:19:43,348
<i>sundae </i>and <i>makjang </i>are always a given.

509
00:19:43,415 --> 00:19:45,551
But all I got was salt in Seoul.

510
00:19:45,617 --> 00:19:47,553
You must've been surprised
when you first got it.

511
00:19:47,619 --> 00:19:49,421
I told them something was missing,

512
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:50,923
that the sauce wasn't here.

513
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:52,257
HOW CUTE

514
00:19:52,324 --> 00:19:53,625
We don't serve it here.

515
00:19:53,692 --> 00:19:56,795
I'm always like,
"How do you eat this? It's so bland."

516
00:19:58,230 --> 00:19:59,431
WINTER'S DIALECT SLIPS OUT

517
00:19:59,498 --> 00:20:02,067
-"How do you eat this…"
-We're hearing the dialect now.

518
00:20:02,134 --> 00:20:04,236
"How do you eat this?"

519
00:20:04,303 --> 00:20:06,371
It tasted so bland.

520
00:20:06,438 --> 00:20:08,207
Do you get self-conscious
when you use your dialect?

521
00:20:08,273 --> 00:20:11,176
-Just a little.
-A little bit? I see.

522
00:20:11,243 --> 00:20:12,578
What are these? Pumpkin leaves.

523
00:20:12,644 --> 00:20:14,713
-Pumpkin leaves?
-You have pumpkin leaves?

524
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:18,350
They're delicious when blanched,
when you use it as wrap for rice…

525
00:20:18,417 --> 00:20:20,986
-Pumpkin leaves and rice?
-…and <i>gang-doenjang</i>, a <i>doenjang </i>dish.

526
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:23,322
People who are older than you
usually enjoy these veggie wraps.

527
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:25,390
I hear that I eat like a granny.

528
00:20:25,457 --> 00:20:27,593
-You eat like a granny?
-A granny?

529
00:20:27,659 --> 00:20:29,027
Not like a baby, but like a granny?

530
00:20:29,094 --> 00:20:30,495
It's an emergency.

531
00:20:30,562 --> 00:20:31,830
I like earthy, hearty dishes

532
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:35,067
like <i>doenjang, cheonggukjang, biji-jjigae,</i>

533
00:20:35,133 --> 00:20:36,768
and even <i>kong-guksu</i>, cold soybean noodles.

534
00:20:36,835 --> 00:20:38,770
-She eats like a granny.
-Like a granny.

535
00:20:38,837 --> 00:20:40,072
Soybean leaves.

536
00:20:40,138 --> 00:20:41,373
-Whoa.
-Soybean leaves.

537
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:44,376
-Really?
-I can easily finish a bowl of white rice

538
00:20:44,443 --> 00:20:45,510
with those pickled leaves.

539
00:20:45,577 --> 00:20:47,179
Perilla leaves.
She really loves things like these.

540
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:49,514
-You do eat like a granny.
-She does.

541
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:51,617
<i>Tteok</i>, rice cake. Do you enjoy these?

542
00:20:51,683 --> 00:20:53,986
I often get my food delivered,

543
00:20:54,052 --> 00:20:55,387
but I'm so impatient

544
00:20:55,454 --> 00:20:56,955
and can't wait that long.

545
00:20:57,022 --> 00:20:59,324
-I have to snack on something.
-I see.

546
00:20:59,391 --> 00:21:00,659
-After ordering a meal?
-Yes.

547
00:21:00,726 --> 00:21:03,962
I always need ice cream,
chips, or even <i>tteok</i>

548
00:21:04,029 --> 00:21:06,231
to snack on while I wait.

549
00:21:06,298 --> 00:21:09,334
But you wouldn't be able
to eat your meal after snacking.

550
00:21:09,401 --> 00:21:11,570
-I still eat.
-Are you the type

551
00:21:11,637 --> 00:21:13,138
who eats small portions often?

552
00:21:13,205 --> 00:21:14,406
If we were runners,

553
00:21:14,473 --> 00:21:16,541
I'd be considered a sprinter.

554
00:21:16,608 --> 00:21:19,177
I like to scarf it all up
and then call it to an end.

555
00:21:19,244 --> 00:21:21,780
But WINTER is a marathoner.

556
00:21:21,847 --> 00:21:24,016
-Eating constantly?
-She keeps eating little by little.

557
00:21:24,082 --> 00:21:26,051
She's Usain Bolt, and she's Lee Bong-ju.

558
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:28,186
DEFINITELY DIFFERENT EVENTS

559
00:21:28,253 --> 00:21:31,189
When people like these eat together,

560
00:21:31,256 --> 00:21:32,224
they can end up fighting.

561
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,392
YOU'RE RIGHT

562
00:21:33,458 --> 00:21:35,193
-She'd have to wait for her.
-Yes.

563
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:37,929
When I feel full while eating my meal,

564
00:21:37,996 --> 00:21:39,931
I take a break before I start over.

565
00:21:39,998 --> 00:21:42,367
Because the food goes down a little
after some time.

566
00:21:42,434 --> 00:21:43,802
By the time I go back,

567
00:21:43,869 --> 00:21:46,204
-she'd be cleaning up.
-I'd clean up.

568
00:21:46,271 --> 00:21:49,074
I often had to stop her like,
"I'm not done yet!"

569
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:50,575
What do you usually order?

570
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:53,812
-I've been hooked on <i>mala xiang guo.</i>
<i>-Mala xiang guo.</i>

571
00:21:53,879 --> 00:21:56,014
-You even have this sauce.
-I do.

572
00:21:56,081 --> 00:21:59,117
-<i>Fen haozi</i> noodles and all.
-She has it all.

573
00:21:59,184 --> 00:22:01,253
When you order those noodles,

574
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:04,256
just two strands of those
would cost me 5,000 won.

575
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:06,558
-They're expensive.
-It's not cost-effective,

576
00:22:06,625 --> 00:22:09,261
so I decided to buy it myself
and add it to the dish,

577
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:11,830
because I was going to order a lot anyway.

578
00:22:11,897 --> 00:22:14,733
-You're frugal.
-She is.

579
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:16,234
Is aespa not doing well financially?

580
00:22:17,069 --> 00:22:18,937
That's not the reason.

581
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:21,606
She's thrifty and knows how to save money.
It's great.

582
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:22,774
Actually, those noodles

583
00:22:22,841 --> 00:22:25,377
are usually kept in the freezer.

584
00:22:25,444 --> 00:22:26,845
But like I said, I'm impatient,

585
00:22:26,912 --> 00:22:30,816
and they take too long to thaw.

586
00:22:30,882 --> 00:22:35,387
I end up eating <i>tteok</i> and ice cream
while I wait for those to thaw.

587
00:22:35,454 --> 00:22:37,589
-You are impatient.
-A bit.

588
00:22:37,656 --> 00:22:39,424
Wait a second.

589
00:22:39,991 --> 00:22:42,327
Are these all yours?

590
00:22:42,394 --> 00:22:44,196
Because KARINA's are over there, right?

591
00:22:44,262 --> 00:22:45,731
-There's… <i>Makgeolli.</i>
-Everything!

592
00:22:45,797 --> 00:22:48,433
Beer, champagne, and wine.

593
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:50,769
-You have every kind.
-And soju.

594
00:22:50,836 --> 00:22:52,738
-She failed to open this on the first try.
-This?

595
00:22:52,804 --> 00:22:56,341
She failed and broke the cork,
so she cut it in half.

596
00:22:56,408 --> 00:22:58,910
I can't take my alcohol too well,

597
00:22:58,977 --> 00:23:00,412
but I still enjoy a bit of it.

598
00:23:00,479 --> 00:23:02,147
-A drink with your meals?
-Like that.

599
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:04,282
-With your food?
-Yes, with my food.

600
00:23:04,349 --> 00:23:06,585
-She likes a drink with her meals.
-But wait.

601
00:23:06,651 --> 00:23:08,653
-She eats like a granny.
-A granny. That's why.

602
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:11,690
-You drink soju with your food?
-She drinks soju and <i>makgeolli</i>.

603
00:23:11,757 --> 00:23:14,126
-Look. She's not done with it.
-She's not.

604
00:23:14,192 --> 00:23:16,161
She puts the lid back on
after drinking some.

605
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:20,265
Wait, the writer clearly said
they'd replace them with new bottles.

606
00:23:20,665 --> 00:23:23,168
EVERYTHING ON CHEF & MY FRIDGE IS CANDID

607
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:25,103
How long did it take to drink this much?

608
00:23:25,170 --> 00:23:28,140
-I had that much in a day.
-In a day.

609
00:23:28,206 --> 00:23:29,141
-Alone?
-A day.

610
00:23:29,207 --> 00:23:30,542
-Alone.
-It happens.

611
00:23:30,609 --> 00:23:32,277
Are you doing okay?

612
00:23:32,344 --> 00:23:34,579
What's important here
is that you had a drink of soju

613
00:23:34,646 --> 00:23:36,214
while eating your meal alone at home.

614
00:23:36,715 --> 00:23:39,217
A COMFORT DRINK AFTER A TOUGH DAY

615
00:23:39,584 --> 00:23:41,520
SO HOMEY

616
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:42,954
She had it alone.

617
00:23:43,021 --> 00:23:44,089
Yes, sitting like a granny.

618
00:23:44,156 --> 00:23:45,957
With rice wrapped in soybean leaves.

619
00:23:46,024 --> 00:23:47,859
Like, "Why isn't KARINA home yet?"

620
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:51,229
-That's Yangsan style.
-Yangsan style.

621
00:23:51,296 --> 00:23:52,864
It feels so approachable and nice.

622
00:23:52,931 --> 00:23:56,334
Then do you two ever drink together?

623
00:23:56,401 --> 00:23:59,237
There's a bench
in front of our dorm building,

624
00:23:59,304 --> 00:24:01,940
-and we had beer there,
-A can of beer.

625
00:24:02,007 --> 00:24:05,310
…with some gummy candy
we got at a convenience store and chatted.

626
00:24:05,377 --> 00:24:07,345
Who can drink alcohol better?

627
00:24:07,412 --> 00:24:08,513
Goodness.

628
00:24:08,580 --> 00:24:10,482
-I wouldn't even dare.
-You wouldn't dare?

629
00:24:10,949 --> 00:24:14,319
KARINA IS FAMOUS AS SOMEONE
WHO CAN HOLD HER LIQUOR

630
00:24:14,386 --> 00:24:17,222
-You must like noodles too.
-I do.

631
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:19,090
What's your favorite noodle dish?

632
00:24:19,157 --> 00:24:22,527
In the end, my favorite
noodle dish has to be pasta.

633
00:24:22,594 --> 00:24:24,596
-I found some pasta sauce.
-Tomato sauce.

634
00:24:24,663 --> 00:24:26,198
-You're right.
-Did you make some?

635
00:24:26,264 --> 00:24:28,667
-No, not yet.
-She has it but doesn't exactly cook.

636
00:24:28,733 --> 00:24:32,137
-She bought all these but never used them.
-She just felt motivated.

637
00:24:32,204 --> 00:24:34,940
Our promotion just ended
after spending many busy days,

638
00:24:35,006 --> 00:24:36,641
and we couldn't even return to the dorm,

639
00:24:36,708 --> 00:24:38,677
so I forgot about the stuff
that I ordered.

640
00:24:38,743 --> 00:24:40,979
-She had been busy.
-All she had was soju and…

641
00:24:41,046 --> 00:24:42,347
JUST A GLASS OF SOJU?

642
00:24:42,414 --> 00:24:44,249
Just soju, and nothing else?

643
00:24:44,316 --> 00:24:45,650
That's kind of sexy.

644
00:24:45,717 --> 00:24:47,219
Without any food?

645
00:24:47,285 --> 00:24:49,387
-I do eat snacks.
-With your meal?

646
00:24:49,454 --> 00:24:51,022
-You know, like kimchi.
-Kimchi?

647
00:24:51,089 --> 00:24:53,625
-Soybean leaves?
-Kimchi?

648
00:24:53,692 --> 00:24:56,528
You're that type?
Soju and kimchi are the real deal.

649
00:24:56,595 --> 00:24:58,797
-I have a question.
-Soju and kimchi?

650
00:24:58,864 --> 00:25:00,866
Do you pour your drink into a glass?

651
00:25:00,932 --> 00:25:04,436
-Then would she drink out of the bottle?
-Out of the bottle.

652
00:25:04,603 --> 00:25:05,837
TELL ME ABOUT IT

653
00:25:07,506 --> 00:25:08,707
-Only she knows.
-But wait.

654
00:25:08,773 --> 00:25:10,342
Do you all pour your drinks

655
00:25:11,276 --> 00:25:12,944
even when you drink alone?

656
00:25:14,746 --> 00:25:17,015
INTERPRETATION: OR IS IT JUST ME?

657
00:25:17,082 --> 00:25:19,518
-I was just curious.
-You drink it out of the bottle?

658
00:25:19,584 --> 00:25:22,020
She'd throw the bottle and go,
"Let me grab some kimchi."

659
00:25:22,087 --> 00:25:23,321
WINTER AT HOME AFTER WORK

660
00:25:23,388 --> 00:25:26,825
GRANNY, IT'S NICE TO DRINK ALONE,
BUT DO LOOK AFTER YOUR HEALTH

661
00:25:26,892 --> 00:25:28,260
Do you enjoy meat?

662
00:25:28,326 --> 00:25:30,395
Yes, I eat meat rather often.

663
00:25:30,462 --> 00:25:33,765
From what I heard,
WINTER would do the grilling

664
00:25:33,832 --> 00:25:36,034
when the members eat meat together.

665
00:25:36,101 --> 00:25:37,168
-Yes.
-It's because

666
00:25:37,235 --> 00:25:39,538
I'm that impatient.

667
00:25:39,604 --> 00:25:44,543
As the most impatient one,
I grill it quickly so I can eat it.

668
00:25:44,609 --> 00:25:47,412
I go, "Do you want this?
No? Then I'll eat it."

669
00:25:47,479 --> 00:25:50,849
I personally don't like to grill meat,

670
00:25:50,916 --> 00:25:52,884
so when she does it next to me, I go,

671
00:25:52,951 --> 00:25:56,321
"This is so delicious. You're so good!"
And she gets very excited.

672
00:25:56,388 --> 00:25:57,822
She goes, "Do you want more?"

673
00:25:58,523 --> 00:25:59,824
"Am I good?"

674
00:25:59,891 --> 00:26:02,027
You're trying to control her.

675
00:26:02,093 --> 00:26:04,663
Not only are you impatient,
you've been praised into doing it.

676
00:26:04,729 --> 00:26:07,299
-What could this be?
-It's frozen.

677
00:26:07,365 --> 00:26:09,901
-<i>Gejang, </i>seasoned raw crab, in soy sauce?
-<i>Gejang </i>in soy sauce.

678
00:26:09,968 --> 00:26:12,971
-My mom told me to keep it frozen.
-I wouldn't be able to hold myself back.

679
00:26:13,038 --> 00:26:16,007
But I can't wait until it thaws,
so I haven't had it yet.

680
00:26:16,441 --> 00:26:18,176
PLEASE GET BETTER

681
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:19,644
When you freeze it,

682
00:26:19,711 --> 00:26:21,813
it's better to separate
the crabs from the sauce.

683
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:24,382
-Really?
-You can keep sauce in the kimchi fridge

684
00:26:24,449 --> 00:26:27,319
and freeze the crabs separately.
That way, they'll thaw faster.

685
00:26:27,385 --> 00:26:30,055
I see. That's a great life hack.

686
00:26:30,121 --> 00:26:32,657
-So she's never had this.
-If you hate thawing that much,

687
00:26:32,724 --> 00:26:34,559
just leave the freezer open
when you leave.

688
00:26:34,893 --> 00:26:35,860
ANOTHER GREAT LIFE HACK?

689
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:37,395
It'll be thawed when you get home.

690
00:26:37,462 --> 00:26:40,065
She can't do that.

691
00:26:40,131 --> 00:26:43,201
She's way more impatient than I thought.

692
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:44,869
Especially when I'm hungry,

693
00:26:44,936 --> 00:26:47,172
because I want
to eat something immediately.

694
00:26:47,238 --> 00:26:49,374
I can't contain my hunger.

695
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:51,343
That must be why you like our show.

696
00:26:51,409 --> 00:26:54,512
-Everything is so quick.
-In just 15 minutes.

697
00:26:54,579 --> 00:26:56,448
-Right?
-Yes, so I love it.

698
00:26:56,514 --> 00:27:00,085
We'll cook delicious meals for you
in just 15 minutes today.

699
00:27:00,151 --> 00:27:02,253
That's all for WINTER's fridge!

700
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:04,723
-I didn't know she was impatient.
-Me neither.

701
00:27:04,789 --> 00:27:07,792
Wait, so do all of you…

702
00:27:07,859 --> 00:27:09,361
always pour it into a glass?

703
00:27:09,427 --> 00:27:11,129
When it comes to soju, usually, yes.

704
00:27:11,429 --> 00:27:13,665
OH, I SEE

705
00:27:13,732 --> 00:27:19,004
I wonder what WINTER
is looking to eat on the show today.

706
00:27:19,070 --> 00:27:21,172
Let's find out her orders. Show us!

707
00:27:21,239 --> 00:27:23,942
These are WINTER's orders.

708
00:27:24,009 --> 00:27:25,677
Both of them are revealed at once.

709
00:27:25,744 --> 00:27:29,214
Noodle Dish on the Next Level.

710
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:31,583
Iron Taste to the Max Level.

711
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:33,318
What does "iron taste" mean?

712
00:27:33,385 --> 00:27:34,586
The taste of metal?

713
00:27:34,653 --> 00:27:37,522
For the first order,
are you looking for a noodle dish?

714
00:27:37,589 --> 00:27:40,091
I love all noodle dishes,

715
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:43,595
but I always end up eating
something that I'm familiar with.

716
00:27:43,662 --> 00:27:47,065
So today, I wanted to eat
a noodle dish on the next level,

717
00:27:47,132 --> 00:27:50,402
-something very special.
-A new noodle dish.

718
00:27:50,468 --> 00:27:52,637
-Not this level, but the next level.
-The next level.

719
00:27:52,704 --> 00:27:56,141
You all saw her hand flip, right?
She wants something on a new level,

720
00:27:56,207 --> 00:27:59,444
something that can flip her world
and show her a new one.

721
00:27:59,511 --> 00:28:02,280
What's the next one?
Iron Taste to the Max Level?

722
00:28:02,347 --> 00:28:04,349
By Iron Taste to the Max Level,

723
00:28:04,416 --> 00:28:06,985
I mean something very intense,
which I've been hooked on.

724
00:28:07,052 --> 00:28:10,221
So I want to eat something intense,
almost metallic or iron-like.

725
00:28:11,756 --> 00:28:13,591
When I hear "iron taste,"

726
00:28:13,658 --> 00:28:16,828
I'm reminded of the taste
of a pull-up bar.

727
00:28:16,895 --> 00:28:19,464
When I was a kid,
occasionally I'd put my tongue on it.

728
00:28:19,698 --> 00:28:21,833
EYES SHUT

729
00:28:21,900 --> 00:28:23,635
Did you need more iron?

730
00:28:23,702 --> 00:28:25,670
I didn't have enough food!

731
00:28:25,737 --> 00:28:28,006
I thought you had an iron deficiency.

732
00:28:28,073 --> 00:28:29,974
Sung-jun, can you tell us about this?

733
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:33,044
Let me share my opinion
as a member of MY, aespa's fan club.

734
00:28:33,111 --> 00:28:34,846
What exactly is an iron taste?

735
00:28:34,913 --> 00:28:36,881
Something bold, charismatic,

736
00:28:36,948 --> 00:28:38,283
and exhilarating.

737
00:28:38,349 --> 00:28:40,719
Those are aespa's stylistic concepts.

738
00:28:40,785 --> 00:28:43,855
Yes, their music is often described
as having an "iron taste."

739
00:28:43,922 --> 00:28:45,924
An iron taste, something very intense.

740
00:28:45,990 --> 00:28:48,993
Come to think of it,
shouldn't you jump in, Sung-jun?

741
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:50,495
-You should.
-You know it.

742
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:52,464
-You get it.
-Do you want a chance?

743
00:28:52,530 --> 00:28:54,866
-I'll join the round right away.
-Will you?

744
00:28:55,100 --> 00:28:56,034
GLAD

745
00:28:56,101 --> 00:28:57,202
He understands the order perfectly.

746
00:28:57,268 --> 00:28:59,704
-I'll go with Iron Taste.
-Very well.

747
00:28:59,771 --> 00:29:02,340
Sung-jun joins
Iron Taste to the Max Level.

748
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:04,642
When it comes to an iron taste,

749
00:29:04,709 --> 00:29:07,679
there should be a connection
to the flavor that a knife brings.

750
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:10,615
-She practically dances with her knife.
-Yes.

751
00:29:10,682 --> 00:29:14,486
I'll show her my magic with an iron taste
that my knife can bring out.

752
00:29:16,087 --> 00:29:17,455
So you're up against Sung-jun?

753
00:29:17,522 --> 00:29:19,958
GLARE, WINCING

754
00:29:20,024 --> 00:29:21,993
-Only the noodle round is available now.
-Noodles.

755
00:29:22,060 --> 00:29:24,662
-Noodle Dish on the Next Level.
-There are many candidates.

756
00:29:25,029 --> 00:29:26,131
RAISING HAND!

757
00:29:26,197 --> 00:29:27,298
SQUEAL♥

758
00:29:27,632 --> 00:29:29,200
OH MY

759
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:31,669
-WINTER looks so excited.
-You're so happy.

760
00:29:31,736 --> 00:29:34,038
-He wants to be her teacher.
-That's true.

761
00:29:34,372 --> 00:29:36,474
HOPING TO BE WINTER'S TEACHER

762
00:29:36,541 --> 00:29:37,375
"Be my student."

763
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:39,177
-You're right.
-"The teacher."

764
00:29:39,244 --> 00:29:41,579
Who wants to fight Sam and make noodles?

765
00:29:41,646 --> 00:29:43,848
I'll go.

766
00:29:44,115 --> 00:29:45,483
WELCOME

767
00:29:45,550 --> 00:29:47,118
This is quite hard to do.

768
00:29:47,185 --> 00:29:49,220
The contenders have been decided.

769
00:29:49,287 --> 00:29:52,290
Noodle Dish on the Next Level
just for WINTER.

770
00:29:52,357 --> 00:29:55,326
Let us begin the round
between Sam and Ho-young!

771
00:29:57,729 --> 00:30:01,933
<i>The first round of cook-off</i>
<i>played with WINTER's ingredients.</i>

772
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:05,937
Chef Jung Ho-young, who's now unable
to cook without Sam, is up.

773
00:30:06,204 --> 00:30:07,272
THE FANS ARE AMUSED

774
00:30:07,338 --> 00:30:11,776
And up against him is Chef Sam Kim,
who now refuses to be his kitchen toolman.

775
00:30:11,843 --> 00:30:13,178
My masters are competing.

776
00:30:13,244 --> 00:30:15,547
You two are currently tied in this season,

777
00:30:15,613 --> 00:30:18,216
both with six wins and six losses,

778
00:30:18,283 --> 00:30:19,484
making the winning rate 50%.

779
00:30:19,551 --> 00:30:22,921
But Chef Sam has recently lost
three times in a row,

780
00:30:22,987 --> 00:30:25,423
whereas Chef Ho-young
has won three consecutive rounds.

781
00:30:25,490 --> 00:30:28,459
-Different momentum levels.
-That's how they're tied now.

782
00:30:28,526 --> 00:30:31,029
On top of that,
in their most recent cook-off,

783
00:30:31,095 --> 00:30:32,330
Chef Ho-young had won.

784
00:30:32,764 --> 00:30:34,499
EP. LEE JUN-YOUNG,
WHEN LIFE HOOKS YOU ON RAMEN

785
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:36,668
SAM'S BASIL RAMEN
VS. HO-YOUNG'S MERINGUE RAMEN

786
00:30:37,001 --> 00:30:39,103
THE RAMEN ROUND ENDED
IN HO-YOUNG'S VICTORY

787
00:30:39,370 --> 00:30:41,639
Sam had been waiting
to get his revenge since that day.

788
00:30:41,706 --> 00:30:44,609
He has even sharpened his canine
in preparation.

789
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:48,146
The day of that ramen cook-off

790
00:30:48,213 --> 00:30:52,217
-was the first time I had made ramen.
-Right. That was the case.

791
00:30:52,283 --> 00:30:54,853
But he probably makes ramen every day.

792
00:30:54,919 --> 00:30:56,287
-Right.
-"Every day"?

793
00:30:56,354 --> 00:30:58,790
-So it did feel a little unfair.
-Did it?

794
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:00,558
If I make pasta today

795
00:31:00,625 --> 00:31:02,327
and beat Sam,

796
00:31:02,393 --> 00:31:05,463
-he won't have anything to complain about.
-He can't complain.

797
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:07,532
So I will make pasta today.

798
00:31:08,366 --> 00:31:09,567
-Are you making pasta?
-Yes.

799
00:31:09,634 --> 00:31:10,802
That's a big decision.

800
00:31:10,869 --> 00:31:11,769
INHALING

801
00:31:11,836 --> 00:31:12,670
Oh, come on.

802
00:31:12,737 --> 00:31:15,473
What if Sam doesn't make pasta?

803
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:17,542
That would mean he chickened out.

804
00:31:17,609 --> 00:31:19,077
Yes, it'd mean he's a chicken.

805
00:31:19,143 --> 00:31:20,078
Scared?

806
00:31:21,079 --> 00:31:22,447
I will make pasta.

807
00:31:22,513 --> 00:31:24,382
-Pasta?
-You'll make pasta?

808
00:31:24,449 --> 00:31:25,617
A head-on match.

809
00:31:25,683 --> 00:31:26,784
I'll just win.

810
00:31:26,851 --> 00:31:29,888
Yes, exactly. You can just win.

811
00:31:29,954 --> 00:31:33,024
But the problem is that
aespa currently seems to favor Ho-young,

812
00:31:33,091 --> 00:31:34,459
almost as their fifth member.

813
00:31:34,525 --> 00:31:37,629
-Because I did their dance three times.
-Yeah, sure.

814
00:31:37,695 --> 00:31:38,696
However,

815
00:31:38,763 --> 00:31:41,199
Sam quickly made his case too.

816
00:31:41,266 --> 00:31:43,601
That he also did aespa's dance?

817
00:31:43,668 --> 00:31:45,703
-You did their dance?
-I did.

818
00:31:45,770 --> 00:31:48,506
Ho-young always dances
like it's a routine.

819
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:50,642
-But I do it only once in a while.
-True.

820
00:31:50,708 --> 00:31:52,343
-Yes, but when was it?
-I did the dance

821
00:31:52,410 --> 00:31:54,479
to "Whiplash"
for Wrap-Wrap-Wrap-Wrap-lash.

822
00:31:54,545 --> 00:31:57,482
YES, RIGHT

823
00:31:57,548 --> 00:31:59,250
Ho-young is the show's KARINA,

824
00:31:59,317 --> 00:32:01,886
-and Sam is the show's WINTER.
-That's the case now.

825
00:32:01,953 --> 00:32:04,222
Before we begin the cook-off,
let me tell you

826
00:32:04,289 --> 00:32:07,926
that the winners of this episode
and the next will get a special prize.

827
00:32:07,992 --> 00:32:11,429
<i>Chef & My Fridge</i> now has
an official premium tableware set.

828
00:32:11,729 --> 00:32:13,498
TA-DA

829
00:32:13,564 --> 00:32:15,833
But only the winners will get it.

830
00:32:15,900 --> 00:32:17,101
ONLY THE WINNERS GET THE PRIZE

831
00:32:17,168 --> 00:32:19,237
WHO'LL WIN THE TABLEWARE SET?

832
00:32:20,171 --> 00:32:22,073
CHEF HO-YOUNG'S INGREDIENTS:
PASTA, BACON, SHRIMP, MILK

833
00:32:22,140 --> 00:32:24,242
CREAM SAUCE, UDON MEAL KIT,
OYSTER SAUCE, PARMESAN, AND MORE

834
00:32:24,309 --> 00:32:26,711
What are you making, Ho-young?

835
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:29,113
The name of my dish is as follows.

836
00:32:29,180 --> 00:32:32,016
<i>Sam Kim, Beat It, Beat It, Beat It</i>

837
00:32:32,684 --> 00:32:33,918
DISSING HIM WITH A SMILE

838
00:32:34,218 --> 00:32:35,954
HIS DANCE ATTACK IS ON THE NEXT LEVEL

839
00:32:36,554 --> 00:32:37,522
SHOCKED

840
00:32:37,722 --> 00:32:38,656
LAUGHING OUT LOUD

841
00:32:38,723 --> 00:32:40,525
-I see.
-It's called

842
00:32:40,591 --> 00:32:42,593
-Sam Kim, Beat It.
-Beat It.

843
00:32:42,827 --> 00:32:43,728
APPROVED

844
00:32:44,662 --> 00:32:45,930
How is your dish prepared?

845
00:32:45,997 --> 00:32:49,100
I'm going to make cream pasta,

846
00:32:49,167 --> 00:32:52,003
but I want to make it cold.

847
00:32:52,070 --> 00:32:54,005
-Cold cream pasta?
-That's what I'm making.

848
00:32:54,072 --> 00:32:57,442
I'll serve it with your mother's <i>gejang</i>
and let you mix it into the sauce

849
00:32:57,508 --> 00:32:59,210
-when you eat it.
-That sounds good.

850
00:32:59,277 --> 00:33:00,611
That sounds delicious.

851
00:33:00,678 --> 00:33:02,647
If I have enough time,

852
00:33:02,714 --> 00:33:04,115
I saw that you had a mango,

853
00:33:04,182 --> 00:33:07,051
-so I'll serve it with mango <i>bingsu</i>.
-Mango <i>bingsu</i> too?

854
00:33:07,919 --> 00:33:09,087
-Sounds good.
-I'll serve those.

855
00:33:09,153 --> 00:33:10,088
JEALOUS

856
00:33:11,022 --> 00:33:12,890
CHEF SAM'S INGREDIENTS:
BACON, MILK, PARMESAN

857
00:33:12,957 --> 00:33:15,093
POTATO, STRIP LOIN, ENOKI,
CREAM SAUCE, TRUFFLE OIL

858
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,729
What are you making, Chef Sam?

859
00:33:18,096 --> 00:33:19,697
WHAT'S SAM'S NOODLE DISH?

860
00:33:19,764 --> 00:33:20,598
He cleared his throat.

861
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:22,166
My dish is called…

862
00:33:24,035 --> 00:33:26,270
<i>Su-Su-Su-Super Fresh Pasta</i>

863
00:33:26,571 --> 00:33:28,373
MOVED

864
00:33:28,673 --> 00:33:30,041
THE ORIGINAL
SU-SU-SU-SUPER UDON

865
00:33:30,541 --> 00:33:32,677
THE SHY SUPER FRESH PASTA

866
00:33:33,711 --> 00:33:35,179
HE MUST GIVE IT TO HIM

867
00:33:35,246 --> 00:33:39,350
-He's making fresh pasta.
-Su-Su-Su-Super Fresh Pasta.

868
00:33:39,417 --> 00:33:40,518
He'll make the pasta noodles.

869
00:33:40,585 --> 00:33:43,254
There's the meat filling
that goes into lasagna,

870
00:33:43,321 --> 00:33:44,789
and I'll serve it with pasta.

871
00:33:45,356 --> 00:33:46,691
It will taste like lasagna,

872
00:33:46,758 --> 00:33:49,927
but I'll throw in some potatoes

873
00:33:49,994 --> 00:33:51,529
and make the sauce thicker.

874
00:33:51,596 --> 00:33:53,498
-Everything is better with potatoes.
-I'll do that.

875
00:33:53,564 --> 00:33:55,066
Also, especially for this,

876
00:33:55,967 --> 00:33:57,435
I won't use dried pasta like that.

877
00:33:57,502 --> 00:33:59,137
SUDDENLY ATTACKS HIS INGREDIENT

878
00:33:59,470 --> 00:34:00,938
WHAT'S SO BAD ABOUT MY DRIED PASTA?

879
00:34:01,005 --> 00:34:03,007
-"Dried pasta like that."
-"Like that."

880
00:34:03,074 --> 00:34:05,676
He picked it out for me
and told me it was the best pasta,

881
00:34:05,743 --> 00:34:07,478
-but now he's attacking me.
-I heard it too.

882
00:34:07,545 --> 00:34:11,082
Well, that brand is
one of the best dried pastas.

883
00:34:11,482 --> 00:34:12,550
TRYING TO PATCH IT UP…

884
00:34:12,617 --> 00:34:14,352
But is fresh pasta on the next level?

885
00:34:14,419 --> 00:34:16,287
Completely.

886
00:34:16,354 --> 00:34:17,455
Completely.

887
00:34:18,523 --> 00:34:21,125
I'll make wide, flat fresh pasta.

888
00:34:21,192 --> 00:34:23,428
-Wide and flat?
-Once you try it,

889
00:34:23,494 --> 00:34:25,496
for fresh noodles made in 15 minutes,

890
00:34:25,563 --> 00:34:26,998
you'll see that it's on another level.

891
00:34:27,198 --> 00:34:28,266
FEELING BITTER

892
00:34:28,332 --> 00:34:31,169
He says fresh pasta is on the next level.

893
00:34:31,235 --> 00:34:32,270
The next level disease.

894
00:34:32,336 --> 00:34:34,272
Are you just making pasta? Anything else?

895
00:34:34,338 --> 00:34:36,140
No, nothing else.

896
00:34:36,207 --> 00:34:37,175
He's confident.

897
00:34:37,241 --> 00:34:39,811
I'll serve only that
simple yet rich-flavored dish.

898
00:34:40,711 --> 00:34:41,979
-Sounds good.
-Just the pasta.

899
00:34:42,046 --> 00:34:43,915
And now,

900
00:34:43,981 --> 00:34:48,186
let us begin the first round for WINTER,
Noodle Dish on the Next Level.

901
00:34:48,252 --> 00:34:50,188
Give us the timer for 15 minutes.

902
00:34:54,826 --> 00:34:56,360
-Whoa.
-Wow.

903
00:34:56,427 --> 00:34:57,528
I love the vibe.

904
00:34:58,529 --> 00:35:00,398
The dancing machine of the show,

905
00:35:00,465 --> 00:35:01,999
<i>HORINA.</i>

906
00:35:02,066 --> 00:35:03,034
HORINA.

907
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:05,069
-What?
-HORINA.

908
00:35:05,136 --> 00:35:06,237
Chef Jung Ho-young.

909
00:35:07,705 --> 00:35:09,941
<i>The gateway member of the show,</i>

910
00:35:10,508 --> 00:35:11,843
<i>SAMTER.</i>

911
00:35:11,909 --> 00:35:13,845
-SAMTER.
-SAMTER?

912
00:35:13,911 --> 00:35:16,114
-SAMTER?
-Yes, that's right.

913
00:35:16,180 --> 00:35:17,315
Not WINTER, but SAMTER.

914
00:35:17,381 --> 00:35:20,184
It sounds like <i>Saemteo</i>, fountain,
that literary magazine.

915
00:35:20,251 --> 00:35:22,687
HORINA versus SAMTER.

916
00:35:22,753 --> 00:35:25,656
Which chef will show
the next level of noodle dish?

917
00:35:25,723 --> 00:35:28,826
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

918
00:35:30,161 --> 00:35:31,262
LIVE FEED ON

919
00:35:31,329 --> 00:35:33,131
-Wow.
-We can see it like this?

920
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,867
TO KWANGYA!

921
00:35:36,868 --> 00:35:38,336
Starting with salt.

922
00:35:39,003 --> 00:35:40,805
That pasta looked pretty thick.

923
00:35:40,872 --> 00:35:42,773
Is it spaghetti? What is it?

924
00:35:43,274 --> 00:35:44,342
-Everything?
-That much?

925
00:35:44,408 --> 00:35:45,776
-That's too much.
-It is.

926
00:35:45,843 --> 00:35:47,445
They'll stick to one another.

927
00:35:47,512 --> 00:35:48,813
-That's too much.
-It is?

928
00:35:48,880 --> 00:35:50,281
That's a lot.

929
00:35:50,348 --> 00:35:52,150
-That's enough for six.
-Dang it.

930
00:35:52,717 --> 00:35:54,952
-You're breaking it?
-Do that later.

931
00:35:55,019 --> 00:35:56,988
-You're breaking the pasta?
-Later.

932
00:35:57,054 --> 00:35:59,056
Is it okay to push it in like that?

933
00:35:59,123 --> 00:36:02,126
If it's half-immersed
and half out of the pot,

934
00:36:02,193 --> 00:36:03,895
some parts will remain undercooked.

935
00:36:03,961 --> 00:36:05,329
That can happen.

936
00:36:05,396 --> 00:36:07,665
Next, some meat.

937
00:36:07,732 --> 00:36:09,400
-It's bacon.
-Is that bacon?

938
00:36:09,467 --> 00:36:10,368
-Bacon?
-It is.

939
00:36:10,434 --> 00:36:11,903
Cream pasta is often made with bacon.

940
00:36:11,969 --> 00:36:14,539
You have to make a dish on another level.

941
00:36:14,605 --> 00:36:17,074
She has had lots of pasta already.

942
00:36:18,476 --> 00:36:19,410
ON THE PAN

943
00:36:19,477 --> 00:36:20,311
AND IN THE POT

944
00:36:20,378 --> 00:36:22,647
-They're both using bacon.
-They're both using it.

945
00:36:23,381 --> 00:36:24,215
1. COOK BACON AND ONION

946
00:36:24,282 --> 00:36:25,683
They're both using bacon.

947
00:36:25,917 --> 00:36:27,185
NEXT, THE SAUCE!

948
00:36:27,552 --> 00:36:28,386
BUTTER

949
00:36:28,853 --> 00:36:33,257
2. MAKE BÉCHAMEL WITH BUTTER,
FLOUR, MILK, AND PARMESAN

950
00:36:33,324 --> 00:36:35,059
Chef Sam's making béchamel.

951
00:36:35,126 --> 00:36:36,427
Béchamel.

952
00:36:36,727 --> 00:36:38,229
MEANWHILE, HORINA IS…

953
00:36:38,529 --> 00:36:39,897
TOSSING AND TURNING

954
00:36:39,964 --> 00:36:42,934
That pasta is thicker than spaghetti.

955
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:44,936
-It'll take a while.
-Did you pick this on purpose?

956
00:36:45,002 --> 00:36:47,371
-I didn't.
-I don't think it'll cook in 15 minutes.

957
00:36:47,438 --> 00:36:48,706
-It was intentional.
-It's so thick.

958
00:36:48,773 --> 00:36:51,943
-It's not adequate for cold pasta.
-It's not.

959
00:36:52,009 --> 00:36:53,311
Does she have other pasta?

960
00:36:53,377 --> 00:36:55,379
-I don't think it'll work.
-What now?

961
00:36:55,446 --> 00:36:57,782
-It's too late.
-These are…

962
00:36:57,848 --> 00:36:59,684
They're as thick as clothes hangers.

963
00:37:01,819 --> 00:37:03,221
FOR NOW, THE NEXT STEPS…

964
00:37:03,788 --> 00:37:05,723
-Shrimp and milk.
-Milk.

965
00:37:05,790 --> 00:37:07,525
You're just pouring milk over shrimp?

966
00:37:07,592 --> 00:37:08,993
Yes, I poured it in.

967
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:10,728
-Is that mustard?
-Mustard?

968
00:37:10,795 --> 00:37:13,130
-Is that mustard?
-No, it's…

969
00:37:13,197 --> 00:37:14,632
-Peanut butter?
-It's pasta sauce.

970
00:37:14,699 --> 00:37:16,500
-Cream sauce.
-It's cream sauce.

971
00:37:16,567 --> 00:37:18,402
-<i>Tsuyu</i> and oyster sauce.
-<i>Tsuyu.</i>

972
00:37:18,469 --> 00:37:20,771
-That has to be good.
-It has to be.

973
00:37:21,339 --> 00:37:22,974
Master, the pasta isn't in the water.

974
00:37:23,040 --> 00:37:24,775
Wait, these are…

975
00:37:25,343 --> 00:37:27,478
It's been 2 minutes and 30 seconds,
yet it's still hard.

976
00:37:27,545 --> 00:37:28,746
It's an emergency.

977
00:37:28,813 --> 00:37:29,880
THE EMERGENCY MAN CLOCKS IN

978
00:37:29,947 --> 00:37:32,617
-He has to overcook it for cold pasta.
-Exactly.

979
00:37:32,683 --> 00:37:34,952
It'll be too hard
if he cooks it like regular spaghetti.

980
00:37:35,019 --> 00:37:36,454
He'll need 14 minutes to cook that.

981
00:37:36,520 --> 00:37:38,155
It could've been a trap.

982
00:37:38,222 --> 00:37:39,957
He must've picked it out intentionally.

983
00:37:40,024 --> 00:37:42,159
-He wants to win that badly.
-That's my master.

984
00:37:42,226 --> 00:37:43,694
Sam, when will you make your pasta?

985
00:37:43,761 --> 00:37:45,229
Me? I'll have to begin now.

986
00:37:45,296 --> 00:37:46,430
-Right after that?
-Yes.

987
00:37:46,497 --> 00:37:47,832
-Potato first.
-Potato.

988
00:37:47,898 --> 00:37:50,935
-So you're adding that to the sauce?
-Yes.

989
00:37:51,002 --> 00:37:53,237
He's using the microwave to cook it.

990
00:37:53,437 --> 00:37:56,774
STRIP LOIN

991
00:37:57,608 --> 00:37:58,876
GRIND

992
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:01,512
-Is that beef?
-It's beef.

993
00:38:01,846 --> 00:38:02,680
GROUND PEPPER

994
00:38:03,414 --> 00:38:06,250
-They move so quickly.
-Don't they?

995
00:38:06,317 --> 00:38:09,287
The faster you finish your dish,

996
00:38:09,353 --> 00:38:11,822
the more favorable
the impatient WINTER will find you.

997
00:38:11,889 --> 00:38:14,458
If it's too hard to wait,
do you want some <i>tteok?</i>

998
00:38:14,525 --> 00:38:16,427
WANT SOME TTEOK FROM YOUR FRIDGE?

999
00:38:16,494 --> 00:38:17,795
Or ice cream.

1000
00:38:17,862 --> 00:38:22,366
-No, she has to enjoy the dishes later.
-She said she hates waiting.

1001
00:38:22,633 --> 00:38:24,702
HORINA FEELS RUSHED
KNOWING SHE'LL BE WAITING…

1002
00:38:25,036 --> 00:38:26,937
GRATE

1003
00:38:27,972 --> 00:38:29,340
That's a lot.

1004
00:38:29,407 --> 00:38:31,475
Ho-young, isn't that too much cheese?

1005
00:38:31,542 --> 00:38:35,279
It needs a good amount of cheese
to make the sauce thicker and delicious.

1006
00:38:35,346 --> 00:38:36,614
Usually,

1007
00:38:36,681 --> 00:38:38,282
Chef Sam would've been
grating the cheese for him.

1008
00:38:39,383 --> 00:38:40,818
-You're right!
-The help.

1009
00:38:40,885 --> 00:38:42,820
-He doesn't have him.
-His "someone" is unavailable.

1010
00:38:42,887 --> 00:38:45,156
-No one's there.
-It'd be nice if someone could grate this.

1011
00:38:45,423 --> 00:38:47,091
WALKS OVER UNDER A SPELL

1012
00:38:47,158 --> 00:38:48,526
-Should I do it?
-Are you free?

1013
00:38:48,592 --> 00:38:50,528
I'm not. I have to do it too.

1014
00:38:50,761 --> 00:38:51,996
HIS SOMEONE IS ON A STRIKE

1015
00:38:52,296 --> 00:38:53,664
THAT SOMEONE IS NOW GONE

1016
00:38:53,731 --> 00:38:56,167
Stop taking advantage of him.

1017
00:38:56,233 --> 00:38:57,768
WHAT'S SAMTER UP TO AFTER LEAVING HORINA?

1018
00:38:57,968 --> 00:38:58,803
FLOUR, ADD EGG

1019
00:39:00,237 --> 00:39:01,939
MAKING FRESH PASTA DOUGH!

1020
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:03,240
He's making the pasta dough.

1021
00:39:03,941 --> 00:39:04,842
Wow.

1022
00:39:06,677 --> 00:39:08,212
HORINA'S BACON IS DONE

1023
00:39:08,779 --> 00:39:10,448
You're discarding the bacon fat?

1024
00:39:10,514 --> 00:39:12,216
-I'm making cold pasta.
-It's cold.

1025
00:39:12,283 --> 00:39:14,085
-He doesn't need it.
-Because it's cold?

1026
00:39:15,152 --> 00:39:15,986
What's that?

1027
00:39:16,053 --> 00:39:18,289
-I think it's <i>gejang</i> in soy sauce.
-<i>Gejang?</i>

1028
00:39:18,356 --> 00:39:20,891
He's separating just the meat
from the marinated crabs.

1029
00:39:20,958 --> 00:39:23,728
Will <i>gejang </i>in soy sauce
go well with cream sauce?

1030
00:39:23,794 --> 00:39:26,030
-It could be fishy.
-Yes, it can be fishy.

1031
00:39:26,097 --> 00:39:28,499
Are you using the meat too?

1032
00:39:28,566 --> 00:39:31,102
She'll mix it in later before she eats.

1033
00:39:31,168 --> 00:39:33,904
-At the last minute?
-That sounds good.

1034
00:39:35,106 --> 00:39:36,907
Only ten minutes left.

1035
00:39:36,974 --> 00:39:38,642
You have to make fresh pasta.

1036
00:39:38,709 --> 00:39:40,644
Yes, pasta! You have to make pasta!

1037
00:39:40,711 --> 00:39:41,979
He's not making pasta yet.

1038
00:39:42,046 --> 00:39:44,648
-I have to do it now.
-Now? You have to hurry.

1039
00:39:44,715 --> 00:39:46,984
-He just has to flatten it.
-Wait, it looks too wet.

1040
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:48,519
-The dough is too wet.
-It's too wet.

1041
00:39:48,586 --> 00:39:50,354
-It's too wet!
-The dough's too wet!

1042
00:39:50,421 --> 00:39:52,223
I know because I've made pasta.
It's too wet.

1043
00:39:52,289 --> 00:39:54,525
-You're good at pasta.
-I am. It's too wet.

1044
00:39:54,592 --> 00:39:57,161
Wet dough is better than dry. It's safer.

1045
00:39:57,228 --> 00:39:59,363
-A bit safer.
-It's better to be wet.

1046
00:39:59,430 --> 00:40:01,565
That's how he makes pasta.

1047
00:40:01,632 --> 00:40:03,601
It may get stuck on the machine.

1048
00:40:03,667 --> 00:40:05,836
Unlike the pasta sold at supermarkets…

1049
00:40:05,903 --> 00:40:07,171
Is it breaking? Is that okay?

1050
00:40:07,238 --> 00:40:08,539
It's okay.

1051
00:40:08,739 --> 00:40:09,907
SU-SU-SU-SUPER FRESH PASTA

1052
00:40:09,974 --> 00:40:11,809
He's putting lots of work into that pasta.

1053
00:40:11,876 --> 00:40:14,145
Hey, the pasta looks nice.

1054
00:40:14,211 --> 00:40:16,714
-That took a little longer than I thought.
-It did.

1055
00:40:16,781 --> 00:40:18,349
But it cooks faster.

1056
00:40:18,416 --> 00:40:20,117
He flattens the pasta once again.

1057
00:40:20,184 --> 00:40:23,053
It looks nice and firm.

1058
00:40:23,120 --> 00:40:24,722
And he sprinkles some flour.

1059
00:40:25,656 --> 00:40:26,490
It looks good.

1060
00:40:27,491 --> 00:40:28,426
He's cutting it now.

1061
00:40:28,492 --> 00:40:31,896
-Yes, he's cutting the dough.
-It looks nice.

1062
00:40:32,630 --> 00:40:34,331
Didn't you say it'd be wider?

1063
00:40:34,398 --> 00:40:35,433
-Is that wide?
-Yes.

1064
00:40:35,499 --> 00:40:37,601
-It gets bigger as it gets cooked.
-It'll get bigger.

1065
00:40:37,668 --> 00:40:40,070
Sam is our go-to guy for pasta.

1066
00:40:40,137 --> 00:40:42,339
-That's so cool.
-He uses some more flour.

1067
00:40:42,406 --> 00:40:44,175
-It looks similar to mine.
-No.

1068
00:40:44,241 --> 00:40:47,044
-It's like Amy's pasta. No?
-What Amy made was <i>jjajangmyeon.</i>

1069
00:40:47,111 --> 00:40:49,747
-That's fresh pasta.
-That's fresh pasta?

1070
00:40:49,814 --> 00:40:51,182
I should've made it like that.

1071
00:40:51,382 --> 00:40:53,851
WHAT ABOUT HORINA,
WHO DOESN'T SPECIALIZE IN PASTA?

1072
00:40:54,251 --> 00:40:56,520
ADDING STARCH WATER FOR THICKNESS?

1073
00:40:56,587 --> 00:40:58,556
He's cooling the sauce now.

1074
00:40:58,622 --> 00:41:00,191
It reminds me of cream udon.

1075
00:41:00,257 --> 00:41:01,725
-It seems so.
-It's pasta.

1076
00:41:01,792 --> 00:41:03,627
It's udon? It's cream udon.

1077
00:41:03,694 --> 00:41:05,496
-It's udon.
-Cream udon is delicious.

1078
00:41:05,563 --> 00:41:06,697
It's pasta.

1079
00:41:06,764 --> 00:41:07,798
I said it's pasta.

1080
00:41:07,865 --> 00:41:10,401
-Cream udon is delicious.
-Yes, I love it.

1081
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:11,735
Nine minutes left.

1082
00:41:11,802 --> 00:41:14,705
What will he do with that beef?

1083
00:41:15,339 --> 00:41:17,975
I guess he's making ragu
with bacon grease.

1084
00:41:18,042 --> 00:41:22,246
-Is that like ragu?
-Yes, but without tomatoes.

1085
00:41:22,746 --> 00:41:24,415
STEAMED POTATO, OUT

1086
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:26,116
He's so calm.

1087
00:41:27,017 --> 00:41:31,555
4. ADD STEAMED POTATO TO BÉCHAMEL AND BOIL

1088
00:41:32,857 --> 00:41:33,958
Is that ice?

1089
00:41:34,024 --> 00:41:34,959
ICE IN THE BLENDER?

1090
00:41:35,025 --> 00:41:37,461
-What's he grinding with all this noise?
-Ice.

1091
00:41:37,528 --> 00:41:39,430
-It's for <i>bingsu</i>, ice flakes.
-He's making <i>bingsu</i>.

1092
00:41:39,830 --> 00:41:40,664
RIGHT!

1093
00:41:40,731 --> 00:41:43,067
-Mango <i>bingsu.</i>
-Mango <i>bingsu.</i>

1094
00:41:43,133 --> 00:41:44,735
-Vanilla ice cream.
-Vanilla ice cream.

1095
00:41:46,103 --> 00:41:48,539
Have they melted? They're runny.

1096
00:41:48,606 --> 00:41:50,374
3. MIX ICE AND VANILLA ICE CREAM

1097
00:41:50,441 --> 00:41:51,709
WINTER looks excited.

1098
00:41:51,775 --> 00:41:52,776
That's <i>bingsu.</i>

1099
00:41:52,843 --> 00:41:56,313
He'll have to finish first
to let her eat it while it's icy.

1100
00:41:56,380 --> 00:41:58,983
-Seven minutes left.
-Seven minutes.

1101
00:41:59,049 --> 00:42:00,918
-Seven minutes.
-Master, check the pasta.

1102
00:42:01,619 --> 00:42:03,487
-Is it okay?
-Dang it. It's like udon.

1103
00:42:03,554 --> 00:42:05,256
It'll still be a while.

1104
00:42:05,322 --> 00:42:07,124
-It'll be a while.
-Hey, Sam.

1105
00:42:07,191 --> 00:42:08,926
-No, it won't work.
-Eight minutes left.

1106
00:42:08,993 --> 00:42:10,694
No, it's too firm.

1107
00:42:10,761 --> 00:42:12,162
CRUNCH?

1108
00:42:12,229 --> 00:42:13,931
Can you throw one to me?

1109
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:15,533
TRY IT

1110
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:18,002
-It's not done.
-It's not?

1111
00:42:18,068 --> 00:42:20,104
-Sam did this on purpose.
-Is it an emergency?

1112
00:42:20,170 --> 00:42:21,805
It's an emergency.

1113
00:42:21,872 --> 00:42:23,073
-What now?
-Is it an emergency?

1114
00:42:23,140 --> 00:42:24,275
It'll never cook in five.

1115
00:42:24,708 --> 00:42:26,277
CHEWING

1116
00:42:26,810 --> 00:42:29,813
It's just like the pasta Amy Park made.

1117
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:32,850
Just heat up some rice
and serve it as soup!

1118
00:42:32,917 --> 00:42:35,386
-You should microwave the pasta.
-You have no other choice.

1119
00:42:35,452 --> 00:42:37,821
Or <i>ramyeon</i>. Ho-young, use <i>ramyeon </i>noodles.

1120
00:42:37,888 --> 00:42:40,391
-It won't cook in five minutes.
-You have to improvise.

1121
00:42:40,457 --> 00:42:42,026
Then it won't be pasta anymore.

1122
00:42:42,092 --> 00:42:44,795
He can't help it!
It's not going to be done in time.

1123
00:42:44,862 --> 00:42:46,463
You have six minutes left.

1124
00:42:46,530 --> 00:42:50,334
-It won't be done.
-Ho-young, you're losing your golden time!

1125
00:42:51,168 --> 00:42:52,970
No way. It'll never work.

1126
00:42:53,037 --> 00:42:55,205
-How bad is it?
-He has no chance.

1127
00:42:55,272 --> 00:42:57,408
CHEF SEON-YEOP CHECKS IT TOO

1128
00:42:57,474 --> 00:42:58,809
It's way too hard.

1129
00:42:58,876 --> 00:43:01,011
It won't work, right? What do you think?

1130
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:03,280
-It won't.
-It won't, right? It's impossible.

1131
00:43:03,881 --> 00:43:05,249
I can't even peel the mango.

1132
00:43:05,316 --> 00:43:07,484
You have no time to peel the mango!

1133
00:43:07,551 --> 00:43:10,287
-Mangoes aren't important now.
-Mango <i>bingsu </i>isn't important.

1134
00:43:10,354 --> 00:43:11,922
You're competing with a noodle dish.

1135
00:43:11,989 --> 00:43:14,124
It's too hard. It won't be done.

1136
00:43:14,191 --> 00:43:16,226
-Does it feel like raw rice?
-Like electric wire.

1137
00:43:16,293 --> 00:43:18,495
-Electric wire?
-I feel like I'm chewing on a wire.

1138
00:43:18,562 --> 00:43:20,130
The result seems too obvious now.

1139
00:43:20,197 --> 00:43:21,231
Man.

1140
00:43:21,298 --> 00:43:22,833
-Everything is against Ho-young.
-It's Sam.

1141
00:43:22,900 --> 00:43:25,202
This is the best pasta brand.

1142
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:27,504
-He told me to use this.
-He'll lose the noodle dish match.

1143
00:43:27,571 --> 00:43:30,307
-Nice texture though.
-He's having trouble peeling mangoes too.

1144
00:43:30,374 --> 00:43:32,276
-Has he done it before?
-Why is he so slow?

1145
00:43:32,343 --> 00:43:34,211
-It's just hard to peel.
-Sung-ju.

1146
00:43:34,278 --> 00:43:37,281
-It's five. Can you check the dishes?
-Yes, let me run over there.

1147
00:43:37,348 --> 00:43:39,083
-Oh, no!
-It's a noodle dish match!

1148
00:43:39,149 --> 00:43:41,151
Only five minutes remain.

1149
00:43:41,218 --> 00:43:43,354
It's already five minutes.

1150
00:43:43,420 --> 00:43:45,356
What? Already?
He hasn't done anything yet.

1151
00:43:45,422 --> 00:43:47,157
He hasn't. This is really bad!

1152
00:43:47,224 --> 00:43:49,393
It's not too late to switch
to <i>ramyeon</i> noodles!

1153
00:43:49,460 --> 00:43:51,562
-You have to cool that pasta too.
-It's too hectic.

1154
00:43:51,629 --> 00:43:53,731
-It's like that.
-It's tough enough to watch.

1155
00:43:53,797 --> 00:43:55,532
So this is the problem, right?

1156
00:43:55,599 --> 00:43:56,867
Will you try the pasta?

1157
00:43:56,934 --> 00:43:58,035
-Oh, gosh.
-Oh, no.

1158
00:43:58,102 --> 00:44:00,571
It's already requiring
quite an effort to pick this up.

1159
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:01,805
It's the thickest spaghetti there is.

1160
00:44:01,872 --> 00:44:03,707
-Why did Sam recommend this?
-It's not like that.

1161
00:44:03,774 --> 00:44:04,808
It's called chitarra.

1162
00:44:04,875 --> 00:44:08,078
-Sam, why did you recommend this?
-It's not like that.

1163
00:44:08,145 --> 00:44:09,813
Let me try the pasta
with four minutes remaining.

1164
00:44:09,880 --> 00:44:11,315
You don't have to try it.

1165
00:44:11,382 --> 00:44:14,652
-Can he beat Sam with that pasta?
-You don't have to.

1166
00:44:14,718 --> 00:44:15,653
Is it pasta or wire?

1167
00:44:15,719 --> 00:44:17,021
It's a wire.

1168
00:44:17,388 --> 00:44:18,922
OH, NO

1169
00:44:18,989 --> 00:44:21,325
-Gosh, what now?
-Come on, Sam.

1170
00:44:21,392 --> 00:44:23,560
He has four minutes left.

1171
00:44:23,627 --> 00:44:24,695
What now?

1172
00:44:24,762 --> 00:44:26,463
Everything actually happens.

1173
00:44:26,530 --> 00:44:28,298
-It literally does.
-Yes.

1174
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:30,434
FIRST, RETRIEVING THE BINGSU

1175
00:44:31,301 --> 00:44:33,437
You have to make a decision.

1176
00:44:33,504 --> 00:44:36,106
He's done with the <i>bingsu.</i>

1177
00:44:36,607 --> 00:44:37,908
RUSHING

1178
00:44:38,442 --> 00:44:40,911
What now? He only has the mango <i>bingsu.</i>

1179
00:44:40,978 --> 00:44:42,279
What now?

1180
00:44:42,346 --> 00:44:43,514
My heart is racing.

1181
00:44:43,714 --> 00:44:45,049
WHAT'S SAMTER UP TO NOW?

1182
00:44:45,249 --> 00:44:49,219
5. CHOP OFF THE TOP OF ENOKI
AND COOK IN BUTTER

1183
00:44:49,853 --> 00:44:51,455
THE PASTA GARNISH

1184
00:44:52,122 --> 00:44:54,725
ADD POTATO BÉCHAMEL

1185
00:44:55,125 --> 00:44:56,894
That looks good.

1186
00:44:56,960 --> 00:44:59,530
Your pasta will cook in two minutes,
but you still have to hurry.

1187
00:44:59,596 --> 00:45:00,764
He's salting the water.

1188
00:45:00,831 --> 00:45:03,734
-That looks good.
-Sam begins to cook his pasta.

1189
00:45:03,801 --> 00:45:07,237
Chef Ho-young!
Sam has some fresh pasta left, right?

1190
00:45:07,304 --> 00:45:08,605
Borrow some.

1191
00:45:08,672 --> 00:45:09,606
Yes.

1192
00:45:09,673 --> 00:45:10,808
The pasta that someone made.

1193
00:45:11,375 --> 00:45:14,244
RUSHING OVER AT THE TEMPTING SUGGESTION

1194
00:45:14,311 --> 00:45:15,813
-It's not cooked yet.
-Not yet.

1195
00:45:17,681 --> 00:45:18,716
LET ME BORROW SOME PASTA

1196
00:45:19,883 --> 00:45:21,085
Hey!

1197
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:24,021
IN MY POT

1198
00:45:24,221 --> 00:45:25,889
SAM HAS MADE SOME GOOD NOODLES

1199
00:45:26,457 --> 00:45:29,093
LOST HIS PASTA IN A FLASH

1200
00:45:29,593 --> 00:45:30,594
SEPARATING WITH A STRAINER

1201
00:45:30,661 --> 00:45:32,062
What is this?

1202
00:45:32,129 --> 00:45:33,997
He trusted him too much.

1203
00:45:34,064 --> 00:45:37,201
-WINTER saw it, so she'll be the judge.
-Yes, she'll be the judge.

1204
00:45:37,835 --> 00:45:39,169
GIVING HIM THE REST

1205
00:45:39,236 --> 00:45:41,105
-He's too kind.
-The pasta!

1206
00:45:41,472 --> 00:45:43,040
HE HAS SUCH A GREAT CHARACTER

1207
00:45:43,107 --> 00:45:45,743
He's such a sweet guy.

1208
00:45:45,943 --> 00:45:47,478
THIS IS MORE THAN ENOUGH

1209
00:45:47,544 --> 00:45:50,180
-Let me try the pasta sauce.
-The sauce is important.

1210
00:45:50,414 --> 00:45:51,782
SLURP

1211
00:45:51,849 --> 00:45:54,685
Is that pasta good enough
to recover his pride?

1212
00:45:54,752 --> 00:45:56,353
My heart is racing.

1213
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:58,722
Is that pasta good enough
to recover his pride?

1214
00:45:58,789 --> 00:46:00,691
Sam won.

1215
00:46:01,158 --> 00:46:02,960
IT'S THAT GOOD?

1216
00:46:03,527 --> 00:46:05,229
I don't even smell anything odd.

1217
00:46:05,295 --> 00:46:07,564
It has such a nice and clean taste.

1218
00:46:07,631 --> 00:46:08,665
This is really nice.

1219
00:46:08,932 --> 00:46:13,537
6. MIX WHITE RAGU PASTA
WITH PARMESAN, OLIVE OIL, AND CREAM SAUCE

1220
00:46:13,804 --> 00:46:15,873
DON'T YOU DARE STEP OVER, HORINA

1221
00:46:15,939 --> 00:46:17,574
He has to keep emulsifying.

1222
00:46:17,641 --> 00:46:20,144
-He made white ragu.
-He did.

1223
00:46:20,377 --> 00:46:21,845
HORINA FEELS ANXIOUS…

1224
00:46:21,912 --> 00:46:25,048
4. MIX CRAB MEAT WITH SESAME OIL
AND MAKE GEJANG SAUCE

1225
00:46:25,282 --> 00:46:27,551
WAS I TOO FOCUSED ON DANCING?

1226
00:46:27,618 --> 00:46:29,019
Ho-young faces a crisis.

1227
00:46:29,086 --> 00:46:30,454
I trusted him far too much.

1228
00:46:30,521 --> 00:46:32,222
BETRAYED BY THE TRUSTED SOMEONE

1229
00:46:32,289 --> 00:46:34,057
So I gave you some pasta.

1230
00:46:34,124 --> 00:46:37,561
I hope at least
the sauce is good, Ho-young!

1231
00:46:37,628 --> 00:46:39,163
The cream sauce!

1232
00:46:39,229 --> 00:46:41,231
Is it good enough to beat Sam?

1233
00:46:41,298 --> 00:46:42,599
If it is, he'd feel more wronged.

1234
00:46:42,666 --> 00:46:45,402
-He has a chance.
-He does?

1235
00:46:45,469 --> 00:46:46,570
WHAT A RELIEF

1236
00:46:46,804 --> 00:46:49,072
THE CREAM IS ON THE NEXT LEVEL

1237
00:46:49,139 --> 00:46:51,408
A minute and 30 seconds!

1238
00:46:51,475 --> 00:46:52,709
What a shame, Ho-young.

1239
00:46:52,776 --> 00:46:54,344
Oh, no.

1240
00:46:54,411 --> 00:46:57,514
-Let me check the first pasta.
-Try it.

1241
00:46:57,581 --> 00:46:59,249
I'll check the first pasta.

1242
00:46:59,316 --> 00:47:01,185
-It looks done.
-But it has to be cold.

1243
00:47:01,251 --> 00:47:04,521
Does it still feel like wire?

1244
00:47:04,588 --> 00:47:06,356
-Hey, this might work.
-It might?

1245
00:47:06,423 --> 00:47:08,759
-He has a chance?
-He does.

1246
00:47:08,826 --> 00:47:09,993
Switch it out!

1247
00:47:10,060 --> 00:47:11,161
REMOVES SAM'S PASTA INSTANTLY

1248
00:47:11,228 --> 00:47:12,729
-Hurry.
-I'll fish it out.

1249
00:47:12,796 --> 00:47:14,431
-Just a little more.
-Thirty seconds.

1250
00:47:14,498 --> 00:47:16,500
-Cook it a little longer.
-You got this.

1251
00:47:16,567 --> 00:47:18,235
You have a minute. It's okay.

1252
00:47:18,435 --> 00:47:19,469
IT'S SO DYNAMIC

1253
00:47:19,536 --> 00:47:21,405
Let it cook for 30 more seconds.

1254
00:47:21,471 --> 00:47:24,775
-The pasta.
-Give it back to Sam.

1255
00:47:24,842 --> 00:47:26,944
Take it back, Sam.

1256
00:47:27,010 --> 00:47:28,812
But you took them from me.

1257
00:47:28,879 --> 00:47:30,714
You have a chance.

1258
00:47:30,781 --> 00:47:32,349
Cook it until the last minute.

1259
00:47:32,416 --> 00:47:33,483
I should calm down.

1260
00:47:33,550 --> 00:47:35,052
It's cold pasta. You can go second.

1261
00:47:35,118 --> 00:47:36,019
You should do the rest.

1262
00:47:36,086 --> 00:47:37,788
-Stay calm.
-Stay calm.

1263
00:47:38,121 --> 00:47:41,658
EVERYONE ADDING THEIR TWO CENTS

1264
00:47:41,725 --> 00:47:43,727
It's okay, Ho-young. You got this.

1265
00:47:43,794 --> 00:47:46,897
-I got this.
-He's making cold pasta.

1266
00:47:46,964 --> 00:47:48,765
5. MIX CREAM SAUCE WITH COOKED BACON

1267
00:47:48,832 --> 00:47:50,934
-Make use of your time. Thirty seconds.
-Thirty seconds!

1268
00:47:51,168 --> 00:47:52,436
HEART POUNDING

1269
00:47:52,736 --> 00:47:55,739
SAMTER BEGINS TO PLATE HIS DISH!

1270
00:47:55,806 --> 00:47:57,407
That looks so good.

1271
00:47:58,709 --> 00:48:00,177
Thirty seconds!

1272
00:48:01,378 --> 00:48:02,713
TRUFFLE OIL

1273
00:48:02,779 --> 00:48:04,047
Sam's almost done.

1274
00:48:04,114 --> 00:48:06,283
And he's done!

1275
00:48:06,350 --> 00:48:09,286
SU-SU-SU-SUPER FRESH PASTA IS DONE

1276
00:48:09,353 --> 00:48:11,822
He continues to boil the pasta
over high heat.

1277
00:48:11,889 --> 00:48:13,824
You have 13 seconds, 12 seconds.

1278
00:48:14,057 --> 00:48:15,859
SPIN THE PASTA

1279
00:48:15,926 --> 00:48:17,160
Time to pull them out.

1280
00:48:17,227 --> 00:48:19,129
-Seven. Six.
-Seven. Six.

1281
00:48:19,196 --> 00:48:21,064
-Five. Four.
-Five.

1282
00:48:21,131 --> 00:48:23,133
-Five. Four.
-Five.

1283
00:48:23,200 --> 00:48:26,069
-Three. Two. One.
-Three. Two. One.

1284
00:48:26,136 --> 00:48:29,740
-That's it. That's time.
-It's over.

1285
00:48:29,806 --> 00:48:32,109
-Serve it.
-What a mess. It's okay.

1286
00:48:32,175 --> 00:48:34,077
You can plate the food,

1287
00:48:34,144 --> 00:48:35,913
but you can't make anything new.

1288
00:48:35,979 --> 00:48:38,115
-Wow.
-Wow. That was insane.

1289
00:48:38,181 --> 00:48:41,018
My heart is pounding too much.

1290
00:48:41,585 --> 00:48:44,054
-That pasta takes the longest to cook.
-It did.

1291
00:48:44,121 --> 00:48:45,989
No, it takes 12 minutes.

1292
00:48:46,056 --> 00:48:48,492
Twelve minutes?
But he said he'd make cold pasta!

1293
00:48:49,526 --> 00:48:52,362
You recommended something that takes
12 minutes for a 15-minute cook-off?

1294
00:48:52,429 --> 00:48:54,264
-Did you expect this to happen?
-No.

1295
00:48:54,331 --> 00:48:57,067
-Ho-young blurted out a bad word.
-He had to wash it in cold water.

1296
00:48:57,134 --> 00:48:59,202
Wait a second.
Are you all siding against me?

1297
00:48:59,269 --> 00:49:01,538
Don't you feel bad for Ho-young?

1298
00:49:02,105 --> 00:49:03,640
Do you need help?

1299
00:49:03,707 --> 00:49:06,510
I think the freezer's broken.

1300
00:49:06,576 --> 00:49:08,245
-Is that bingo mangsu?
-Careful.

1301
00:49:08,312 --> 00:49:10,547
-Bingo mangsu?
-Bingo mangsu?

1302
00:49:10,614 --> 00:49:13,383
IT'S MANGO BINGSU…
BINGO MANGSU(!)

1303
00:49:13,784 --> 00:49:16,486
IT SOUNDS A LOT LIKE BINGSU MANGLED

1304
00:49:16,553 --> 00:49:18,722
-That's now called bingo mangsu.
-Bingo mangsu.

1305
00:49:18,789 --> 00:49:20,557
That bingo mangsu looks mangled.

1306
00:49:20,624 --> 00:49:21,959
MANGSU
EASY LIFE IS NEVER FUN

1307
00:49:22,459 --> 00:49:25,495
JUST LIKE GUMMING CHEW OR PEEZE CHIZZA,
IT'S BINGO MANGSU

1308
00:49:25,929 --> 00:49:28,398
BUT THE VISUALS…

1309
00:49:28,465 --> 00:49:30,734
How come this <i>bingsu </i>has all melted?

1310
00:49:31,001 --> 00:49:32,102
MANGLED BINGSU

1311
00:49:32,169 --> 00:49:33,637
The freezer was a problem too!

1312
00:49:34,037 --> 00:49:35,706
HORINA'S ONE UNLUCKY DAY…

1313
00:49:35,772 --> 00:49:38,375
Sound the bell, Ho-young!

1314
00:49:38,442 --> 00:49:39,843
He's done too!

1315
00:49:39,910 --> 00:49:41,979
-It's like <i>hwachae</i>, fruit salad.
-It's <i>hwachae.</i>

1316
00:49:42,045 --> 00:49:43,613
-It's mango <i>hwachae</i>.
-Is that juice?

1317
00:49:43,680 --> 00:49:46,183
-It's mango <i>hwachae</i>.
-It's mango juice.

1318
00:49:46,249 --> 00:49:47,617
MOVING WITH EVERYONE'S ATTENTION

1319
00:49:47,684 --> 00:49:50,187
-Oh, no. Bingo mangsu.
-Bingo mangsu.

1320
00:49:50,821 --> 00:49:52,923
IN THE END, THEY FINISH WITH A HUG

1321
00:49:53,490 --> 00:49:56,026
-This will be you soon.
-She can drink it.

1322
00:49:56,093 --> 00:49:57,327
It smells so good.

1323
00:49:57,394 --> 00:49:59,162
-It does.
-Does it smell delicious?

1324
00:49:59,229 --> 00:50:03,500
Both noodle dishes were made
just for WINTER.

1325
00:50:03,867 --> 00:50:05,335
WOW♥

1326
00:50:05,402 --> 00:50:07,471
Those 15 minutes went by like a storm.

1327
00:50:07,537 --> 00:50:10,273
And I don't think we've ever seen
Chef Ho-young look so distraught.

1328
00:50:10,340 --> 00:50:11,174
It's been a while.

1329
00:50:11,241 --> 00:50:13,010
I think Sam provided the main reason.

1330
00:50:13,076 --> 00:50:14,411
I'm telling you, no.

1331
00:50:14,478 --> 00:50:16,446
As a fellow Italian chef,

1332
00:50:16,513 --> 00:50:19,149
the fact that he recommended
that pasta to make cold pasta

1333
00:50:19,216 --> 00:50:20,117
is simply crazy.

1334
00:50:20,183 --> 00:50:22,519
What are you saying? That's not the case.

1335
00:50:22,586 --> 00:50:24,287
He came to me with that pasta.

1336
00:50:24,354 --> 00:50:27,090
-It couldn't have been a mistake.
-He came and asked if it was good.

1337
00:50:27,157 --> 00:50:29,426
Then you should've stopped him
from using that one.

1338
00:50:29,493 --> 00:50:31,194
I clearly asked him,

1339
00:50:31,261 --> 00:50:33,964
"I want to make a cold pasta.
How's this one?"

1340
00:50:34,031 --> 00:50:35,832
He said,
"It's great. Make sure you use it."

1341
00:50:36,133 --> 00:50:37,667
IT HAS TO BE THIS ONE

1342
00:50:37,734 --> 00:50:40,037
-Sam has changed.
-No.

1343
00:50:40,103 --> 00:50:42,506
-I'm falsely blamed.
-The losing streak did this to him.

1344
00:50:42,572 --> 00:50:43,774
It made him wicked.

1345
00:50:43,840 --> 00:50:47,044
Is the <i>bingsu</i> back in the freezer?

1346
00:50:47,644 --> 00:50:49,379
I think someone melted the ice cream too.

1347
00:50:49,780 --> 00:50:52,182
IT'S JUST NOT HIS DAY…

1348
00:50:52,249 --> 00:50:54,684
-Who was it? Who did that?
-That mango <i>bingsu</i>

1349
00:50:54,751 --> 00:50:57,020
-must've become bingo mangsu.
-Bingo mangsu.

1350
00:50:57,087 --> 00:50:58,388
-Mangsu.
-Now.

1351
00:50:58,455 --> 00:51:01,591
Chef Sam was the first to finish.

1352
00:51:02,325 --> 00:51:07,497
FRESH PASTA WITH WHITE RAGU SAUCE

1353
00:51:08,765 --> 00:51:13,937
CHEF SAM KIM'S SU-SU-SU-SUPER FRESH PASTA

1354
00:51:14,004 --> 00:51:15,105
Wow.

1355
00:51:15,172 --> 00:51:16,873
-Do I just mix everything?
-Please do.

1356
00:51:16,940 --> 00:51:18,041
It looks good.

1357
00:51:18,108 --> 00:51:19,042
It looks good.

1358
00:51:19,109 --> 00:51:22,946
-I really love rich and creamy sauce.
-I see.

1359
00:51:23,013 --> 00:51:24,448
The pasta is rather thick,

1360
00:51:24,514 --> 00:51:27,150
so there's lots of sauce on it too.

1361
00:51:27,217 --> 00:51:28,085
MMM!

1362
00:51:30,687 --> 00:51:31,621
-Must be good.
-It's good.

1363
00:51:31,688 --> 00:51:33,657
Is it? I see.

1364
00:51:34,391 --> 00:51:36,126
How did he do this in 15 minutes?

1365
00:51:36,193 --> 00:51:38,361
Did you use strip loin?

1366
00:51:38,428 --> 00:51:42,532
<i>I mixed ground strip loin and bacon stock.</i>

1367
00:51:42,599 --> 00:51:44,568
It doesn't have any odd smells,

1368
00:51:44,634 --> 00:51:48,939
and the creamy texture
goes very well with the flavor.

1369
00:51:49,005 --> 00:51:51,141
-It's so delicious.
-I see.

1370
00:51:51,208 --> 00:51:54,044
She has already said that it's delicious
about three to four times.

1371
00:51:54,111 --> 00:51:56,446
The noodles are great too.

1372
00:51:56,513 --> 00:51:59,082
-I like the chewy texture.
-Yes.

1373
00:51:59,149 --> 00:52:01,318
-It's so good.
-It must have a bite to it.

1374
00:52:01,384 --> 00:52:03,820
Ho-young should've taken a hint

1375
00:52:03,887 --> 00:52:06,256
when Sam said
he was going to make the pasta.

1376
00:52:06,323 --> 00:52:08,725
The decision will be made
because of the pasta noodles.

1377
00:52:08,792 --> 00:52:10,327
-Competitions can be cold.
-Yes.

1378
00:52:10,393 --> 00:52:12,195
He had no choice
if he wanted to win the star.

1379
00:52:12,262 --> 00:52:14,264
Ho-young was too naive.

1380
00:52:14,331 --> 00:52:16,399
-He was too naive.
-He trusted him.

1381
00:52:16,466 --> 00:52:18,135
Is the pasta chewy?

1382
00:52:18,201 --> 00:52:19,936
It is.

1383
00:52:20,003 --> 00:52:21,905
Something about its texture is really fun,

1384
00:52:21,972 --> 00:52:23,006
so I keep craving more.

1385
00:52:23,840 --> 00:52:25,408
On top of that, the pasta is fun too.

1386
00:52:25,475 --> 00:52:27,844
-It's so good.
-He made it himself, so it must be fun.

1387
00:52:27,911 --> 00:52:30,213
-May I keep working on it?
-As you wish.

1388
00:52:30,280 --> 00:52:32,215
-Is that okay?
-Do you want to go back and forth?

1389
00:52:32,282 --> 00:52:34,384
-I'd love to.
-Really? All right.

1390
00:52:34,451 --> 00:52:36,253
-You can leave it there.
-Really?

1391
00:52:36,319 --> 00:52:37,721
Do you want some <i>tteok </i>during the switch?

1392
00:52:38,121 --> 00:52:39,422
YOU HAVE 20 SECONDS OF WAIT

1393
00:52:39,489 --> 00:52:40,957
It's tough to wait. There's ice cream too.

1394
00:52:41,391 --> 00:52:42,225
I'M FINE!

1395
00:52:42,292 --> 00:52:45,529
Next up, Chef Ho-young's dish.

1396
00:52:45,595 --> 00:52:47,764
-Please be cooked.
-Sam Kim, Beat It.

1397
00:52:48,832 --> 00:52:52,169
COLD CREAM PASTA
WITH GEJANG IN SOY SAUCE ON THE SIDE

1398
00:52:53,970 --> 00:52:55,539
WITH COLD BINGO MANGSU

1399
00:52:56,439 --> 00:52:58,909
CHEF JUNG HO-YOUNG'S SAM KIM, BEAT IT

1400
00:52:58,975 --> 00:53:01,111
Sam Kim, Beat It.

1401
00:53:01,178 --> 00:53:02,045
-Whoa.
-Beat It.

1402
00:53:02,112 --> 00:53:05,415
She'll find out
if the noodles are fully cooked.

1403
00:53:05,482 --> 00:53:08,852
It wasn't so bad
by the time I tried it toward the end.

1404
00:53:08,919 --> 00:53:10,120
I'm dying to find out.

1405
00:53:10,187 --> 00:53:12,389
It was somewhat edible by then.

1406
00:53:12,455 --> 00:53:14,824
I do like my noodles a bit undercooked.

1407
00:53:14,891 --> 00:53:16,393
Really? I see.

1408
00:53:16,459 --> 00:53:18,461
This pasta was served cold.

1409
00:53:18,528 --> 00:53:20,430
It's my first time trying cold pasta.

1410
00:53:20,497 --> 00:53:22,566
-The noodles…
-It won't roll up.

1411
00:53:22,632 --> 00:53:24,901
-A cold cream pasta.
-The pasta won't roll up.

1412
00:53:24,968 --> 00:53:26,836
-Is it still a wire?
-It seems like it.

1413
00:53:26,903 --> 00:53:29,005
If so, you can't roll it up.
Oh, but you did.

1414
00:53:29,072 --> 00:53:30,607
-So with the crab?
-First,

1415
00:53:30,674 --> 00:53:33,443
try it as is,
and then try it with some crab.

1416
00:53:33,877 --> 00:53:36,279
FIRST, THE PASTA ALONE

1417
00:53:37,013 --> 00:53:37,847
CHUCKLE

1418
00:53:39,549 --> 00:53:40,850
-She chuckled.
-Is it undercooked?

1419
00:53:41,251 --> 00:53:42,986
WEE WOO WEE WOO

1420
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:44,955
Hey. Turn that thing off.

1421
00:53:45,021 --> 00:53:48,225
-It's an emergency.
-The pasta isn't fully cooked, right?

1422
00:53:48,291 --> 00:53:49,926
It could get stuck between your teeth.

1423
00:53:49,993 --> 00:53:51,528
-It could be way too good.
-That?

1424
00:53:51,595 --> 00:53:53,763
-Next, with the crab?
-Yes, mix it in.

1425
00:53:54,698 --> 00:53:58,401
That's the <i>gejang </i>in soy sauce
that her mother sent her.

1426
00:53:58,468 --> 00:54:00,303
She ends up eating it like this.

1427
00:54:00,370 --> 00:54:02,939
-I wonder what that mix is like.
-Right?

1428
00:54:03,006 --> 00:54:05,242
-I wonder what it's like.
-It'd go really well together.

1429
00:54:05,308 --> 00:54:06,409
-It looks good.
-Mmm!

1430
00:54:06,476 --> 00:54:07,444
-Huh?
-Huh?

1431
00:54:07,978 --> 00:54:08,845
Mmm!

1432
00:54:09,946 --> 00:54:11,881
-You look surprised.
-They go so well together.

1433
00:54:11,948 --> 00:54:13,416
They go very well?

1434
00:54:13,483 --> 00:54:15,118
We didn't expect that.

1435
00:54:15,185 --> 00:54:18,088
I've never had anything like it.

1436
00:54:18,154 --> 00:54:20,724
-The next level?
-It goes perfectly with the order.

1437
00:54:24,427 --> 00:54:26,696
-It's an emergency for Sam.
-An emergency.

1438
00:54:26,763 --> 00:54:28,465
-Emergency.
-It suits the order better.

1439
00:54:28,531 --> 00:54:30,533
He could've won
if the pasta was fully cooked.

1440
00:54:30,600 --> 00:54:32,369
-The pasta, right?
-Huh? Maybe not.

1441
00:54:32,435 --> 00:54:34,804
-No?
-Have you had it before?

1442
00:54:34,871 --> 00:54:36,706
It somehow tastes like bulgogi.

1443
00:54:36,773 --> 00:54:38,441
-Bulgogi?
-It tastes like a bulgogi burger!

1444
00:54:38,508 --> 00:54:39,743
A bulgogi burger?

1445
00:54:39,809 --> 00:54:41,544
Why does that taste like a bulgogi burger?

1446
00:54:41,611 --> 00:54:46,549
She had good sesame oil,
so I added a drop into the crab.

1447
00:54:46,616 --> 00:54:48,184
-That was why.
-Like teriyaki sauce.

1448
00:54:48,251 --> 00:54:50,153
The pasta wasn't heavily seasoned.

1449
00:54:50,220 --> 00:54:52,455
I think he considered
adding the crab meat.

1450
00:54:52,522 --> 00:54:54,291
I added the savory flavor
with grated cheese.

1451
00:54:54,357 --> 00:54:55,558
-Is it good?
-Yes.

1452
00:54:55,625 --> 00:54:56,893
Is the pasta cooked well?

1453
00:54:56,960 --> 00:54:58,728
The pasta's evenly…

1454
00:54:59,829 --> 00:55:01,464
It's evenly a bit…

1455
00:55:01,531 --> 00:55:03,900
-Evenly undercooked.
-It must be evenly undercooked.

1456
00:55:03,967 --> 00:55:05,568
-Stop eating it, then.
-Evenly undercooked.

1457
00:55:05,635 --> 00:55:06,803
It's evenly undercooked.

1458
00:55:08,405 --> 00:55:10,106
-But it's fine by me.
-Is it?

1459
00:55:10,173 --> 00:55:12,108
It's not so bad for my taste.

1460
00:55:12,175 --> 00:55:13,410
Was this intentional?

1461
00:55:13,476 --> 00:55:15,378
Yes, she seemed to be

1462
00:55:15,445 --> 00:55:17,981
quite impatient,
so I wanted her to chew it well.

1463
00:55:18,048 --> 00:55:20,317
-Because she's impatient,
-To slow her down.

1464
00:55:20,383 --> 00:55:22,652
…she probably has had undercooked pasta.

1465
00:55:22,886 --> 00:55:23,987
GLANCING

1466
00:55:24,287 --> 00:55:25,855
-Let me try that again.
-Going back.

1467
00:55:25,922 --> 00:55:28,325
-She's now…
-It must be hard.

1468
00:55:28,391 --> 00:55:30,493
-Thank you.
-She likes to take her time with meals,

1469
00:55:30,560 --> 00:55:32,629
switching between the dishes.

1470
00:55:32,696 --> 00:55:36,366
-After all, the order is the Next Level.
-Right.

1471
00:55:37,067 --> 00:55:38,635
YUM

1472
00:55:38,702 --> 00:55:42,505
WINTER is putting a lot of emphasis
on how it must be on the next level.

1473
00:55:43,106 --> 00:55:44,240
Mmm.

1474
00:55:45,308 --> 00:55:47,077
The pasta noodles are really delicious.

1475
00:55:47,344 --> 00:55:48,178
GLANCING

1476
00:55:48,244 --> 00:55:50,013
That's hard to beat.

1477
00:55:50,080 --> 00:55:52,048
-I'm torn.
-You are?

1478
00:55:52,115 --> 00:55:53,583
-I still have <i>bingsu</i>.
-Yes.

1479
00:55:53,650 --> 00:55:55,352
-<i>Bingsu.</i>
-Yes, right!

1480
00:55:55,418 --> 00:55:57,087
Is it really <i>bingsu?</i>

1481
00:55:57,153 --> 00:55:58,855
-He's bringing it now.
-Bingo mangsu.

1482
00:55:58,922 --> 00:56:01,491
-Bingo mangsu.
-It has to be delicious.

1483
00:56:01,558 --> 00:56:03,393
-Bring her the bingo mangsu.
-Wait.

1484
00:56:03,460 --> 00:56:04,894
It melted more in the freezer.

1485
00:56:07,063 --> 00:56:08,531
What kind of freezer is that?

1486
00:56:08,598 --> 00:56:10,133
-Is that juice?
-Oh, no.

1487
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:11,868
RUNNY…

1488
00:56:12,435 --> 00:56:13,670
It's so runny.

1489
00:56:13,737 --> 00:56:16,773
Some say that Sam Kim
has cut the power to the freezer.

1490
00:56:17,240 --> 00:56:19,442
A RATHER VICIOUS RUMOR

1491
00:56:19,509 --> 00:56:21,745
-I knew it.
-This vicious rumor is going around.

1492
00:56:22,345 --> 00:56:23,813
SLOSHING

1493
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:25,215
He's like, "Go down, Ho-young."

1494
00:56:25,281 --> 00:56:26,116
It's <i>hwachae</i>.

1495
00:56:26,182 --> 00:56:27,817
-How funny.
-It's actually mango <i>hwachae</i>.

1496
00:56:27,884 --> 00:56:29,686
-Mango <i>hwachae?</i>
-You want that in summer.

1497
00:56:29,753 --> 00:56:31,287
-I added cherries too.
-You called it <i>bingsu.</i>

1498
00:56:31,354 --> 00:56:33,123
-It's <i>hwachae</i>.
-How is it suddenly <i>hwachae?</i>

1499
00:56:33,189 --> 00:56:34,891
You're right.

1500
00:56:34,958 --> 00:56:37,494
Wait, this is just liquid.

1501
00:56:37,560 --> 00:56:38,661
It's liquid, right?

1502
00:56:38,728 --> 00:56:39,829
SLURRRP

1503
00:56:39,896 --> 00:56:41,030
She's drinking it.

1504
00:56:41,097 --> 00:56:42,766
Is it <i>bingsu </i>or mangled <i>bingsu?</i>

1505
00:56:42,832 --> 00:56:44,000
SMACK SMACK

1506
00:56:44,067 --> 00:56:44,968
MMM

1507
00:56:45,034 --> 00:56:46,970
It's something
you can get anywhere, right?

1508
00:56:47,504 --> 00:56:48,338
PFFT!

1509
00:56:48,972 --> 00:56:51,674
The usual mango <i>bingsu</i>
you can now get just about anywhere.

1510
00:56:52,442 --> 00:56:53,276
Vanilla ice cream.

1511
00:56:53,343 --> 00:56:54,878
IT'S JUST ICE CREAM

1512
00:56:54,944 --> 00:56:56,346
The ice cream flavor?

1513
00:56:56,413 --> 00:57:00,016
-The ice cream flavor. Right?
-All he did was blend ice cream with ice.

1514
00:57:00,083 --> 00:57:03,253
-It should've been like <i>bingsu.</i>
-It's now like…

1515
00:57:03,319 --> 00:57:04,621
MMM

1516
00:57:04,687 --> 00:57:07,157
It just tastes like

1517
00:57:07,223 --> 00:57:09,859
-regular mango <i>bingsu</i>.
-It's just mango and ice cream.

1518
00:57:09,926 --> 00:57:11,795
-But it's good. Delicious.
-But it's good.

1519
00:57:11,861 --> 00:57:13,830
That wasn't the main dish.

1520
00:57:13,897 --> 00:57:15,064
-It wasn't.
-What a shame.

1521
00:57:15,131 --> 00:57:18,701
-This is hard.
-She likes this, so it's like a bonus.

1522
00:57:18,768 --> 00:57:22,572
-Let's see KARINA try it while she thinks.
-Yes, some for KARINA.

1523
00:57:22,639 --> 00:57:24,741
Please try Chef Sam's dish first.

1524
00:57:24,808 --> 00:57:26,209
Thank you for the food.

1525
00:57:27,944 --> 00:57:29,846
A BIG BITE

1526
00:57:31,815 --> 00:57:33,316
Mmm!

1527
00:57:33,383 --> 00:57:34,417
Mmm.

1528
00:57:34,984 --> 00:57:36,519
-Mmm.
-She's excited.

1529
00:57:36,586 --> 00:57:37,887
What does that look mean?

1530
00:57:37,954 --> 00:57:40,323
Wait, what's going on?

1531
00:57:40,390 --> 00:57:43,426
-It's so delicious.
-Is it really?

1532
00:57:43,493 --> 00:57:44,894
It's Sam's pasta.

1533
00:57:44,961 --> 00:57:47,797
-This fresh pasta is…
-Different, right?

1534
00:57:47,864 --> 00:57:50,533
Yes, it's a stroke of genius.

1535
00:57:50,600 --> 00:57:54,704
<i>I also love this subtle truffle aroma.</i>

1536
00:57:54,771 --> 00:57:57,907
I'm not so good with truffles,
but this is delicious.

1537
00:57:58,675 --> 00:58:00,376
A BIG BITE

1538
00:58:00,877 --> 00:58:02,245
YUM

1539
00:58:02,312 --> 00:58:03,146
MMM

1540
00:58:03,713 --> 00:58:04,714
She's eating again.

1541
00:58:04,781 --> 00:58:06,916
WINTER'S ON A MARATHON

1542
00:58:06,983 --> 00:58:09,686
-The next one.
-I'm looking forward…

1543
00:58:09,752 --> 00:58:11,254
-…to this one.
-Chef Ho-young's dish,

1544
00:58:11,321 --> 00:58:12,822
Sam Kim, Beat It.

1545
00:58:12,889 --> 00:58:14,791
We have some more of his dish,
so please try some.

1546
00:58:15,358 --> 00:58:18,862
How different is it from the fresh pasta?

1547
00:58:19,462 --> 00:58:21,865
THE RIGHT-HAND CHEFS JOIN THEM

1548
00:58:22,732 --> 00:58:25,168
SLOW, LONG-DISTANCE EATING

1549
00:58:25,568 --> 00:58:27,437
KARINA TAKES A BITE TOO

1550
00:58:29,439 --> 00:58:31,441
-Why? What is it? Is it cooked?
-It's good.

1551
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:32,709
-Is it okay?
-It's good.

1552
00:58:32,775 --> 00:58:34,277
-I see.
-Is it evenly cooked?

1553
00:58:34,344 --> 00:58:36,012
KARINA says it's cooked well.

1554
00:58:36,079 --> 00:58:39,415
-Some time passed, so it's a bit soggier.
-Is that so?

1555
00:58:39,816 --> 00:58:40,817
WINTER CHECKS AGAIN

1556
00:58:40,884 --> 00:58:43,186
It could've become soggier
while WINTER tried some.

1557
00:58:43,253 --> 00:58:45,188
-It's good.
-Yes, it's good.

1558
00:58:45,255 --> 00:58:49,225
We can call this al dente
and say that some will like it.

1559
00:58:49,292 --> 00:58:52,562
-Let me try it with the <i>gejang.</i>
-She's adding the crab this time.

1560
00:58:53,263 --> 00:58:54,397
YUM-YUM

1561
00:58:54,464 --> 00:58:56,566
-It must be so flavorful.
-Cream sauce and soy sauce.

1562
00:58:57,700 --> 00:58:58,868
MMM

1563
00:58:58,935 --> 00:59:00,937
MMM!

1564
00:59:01,004 --> 00:59:03,139
I'm sorry, but tell us
instead of sending signals.

1565
00:59:03,206 --> 00:59:06,543
-What are you two doing?
-You're sending signals to each other.

1566
00:59:06,609 --> 00:59:08,111
When I had it with <i>gejang,</i>

1567
00:59:08,177 --> 00:59:10,813
-the flavor changed 4 times in my mouth.
-It changed 4 times?

1568
00:59:10,880 --> 00:59:12,649
First, it tasted like cream,

1569
00:59:12,715 --> 00:59:14,284
then soy sauce,

1570
00:59:14,350 --> 00:59:17,854
then they mix
into a blend of creamy soy sauce,

1571
00:59:17,921 --> 00:59:19,455
and lastly, like a bulgogi burger.

1572
00:59:19,789 --> 00:59:21,024
THAT'S WHAT WINTER SAID♥

1573
00:59:21,090 --> 00:59:22,592
-Just like what WINTER said.
-Yes.

1574
00:59:22,659 --> 00:59:25,228
The right-hand chefs,
have you tried it too?

1575
00:59:25,295 --> 00:59:27,497
-Yes.
-What did you think?

1576
00:59:27,564 --> 00:59:30,233
They actually made it happen.
I thought it wouldn't come together.

1577
00:59:30,300 --> 00:59:32,802
I see. How did it taste?

1578
00:59:32,869 --> 00:59:35,605
It also came out very delicious.

1579
00:59:36,973 --> 00:59:38,975
Add more details
and tell them why it was good.

1580
00:59:39,242 --> 00:59:40,577
IMMEDIATELY DISCIPLINED

1581
00:59:40,643 --> 00:59:41,744
My gosh.

1582
00:59:41,811 --> 00:59:43,780
Can you do this
in the next episode, Chef Do-hee?

1583
00:59:43,846 --> 00:59:45,882
-I'll try to pull something off.
-You'll try.

1584
00:59:45,949 --> 00:59:47,517
-He's rather frightened.
-He is?

1585
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:48,985
He has now seen the 15 minutes.

1586
00:59:49,586 --> 00:59:51,087
Time flew by too quickly.

1587
00:59:51,154 --> 00:59:52,388
-It does, right?
-It flew by.

1588
00:59:52,455 --> 00:59:54,490
There's a subtle smell of truffle,

1589
00:59:54,557 --> 00:59:59,362
<i>and the mix of </i>gejang <i>in soy sauce,</i>
<i>truffle, and cream sauce</i>

1590
00:59:59,429 --> 01:00:02,632
seemed unlikely at first,
but they work well as a team.

1591
01:00:03,399 --> 01:00:05,234
CONTINUES TO EAT UNTIL THE END

1592
01:00:05,301 --> 01:00:07,837
Even as we chatted,

1593
01:00:07,904 --> 01:00:10,306
WINTER continued to eat her food.

1594
01:00:10,373 --> 01:00:11,541
Have you made a decision?

1595
01:00:11,608 --> 01:00:13,343
-I think so.
-She made her decision.

1596
01:00:13,409 --> 01:00:16,512
The chef who gets chosen by WINTER

1597
01:00:16,579 --> 01:00:21,017
will take both the star
and the tableware set.

1598
01:00:21,084 --> 01:00:23,286
Also, we'll give the winning chef

1599
01:00:23,353 --> 01:00:26,923
another chance to do his dance.

1600
01:00:26,990 --> 01:00:29,225
So who's the winner?

1601
01:00:29,292 --> 01:00:31,294
<i>Press one for Sam Kim.</i>

1602
01:00:31,361 --> 01:00:33,229
<i>Press two for Jung Ho-young.</i>

1603
01:00:33,296 --> 01:00:35,698
If you made your decision,
please press the button.

1604
01:00:37,333 --> 01:00:38,901
Right now.

1605
01:00:38,968 --> 01:00:40,303
-I did.
-You did?

1606
01:00:40,370 --> 01:00:42,071
She made her decision.

1607
01:00:42,138 --> 01:00:44,407
Let's find out WINTER's choice.

1608
01:00:44,474 --> 01:00:46,009
Show us! Which one is it?

1609
01:00:46,743 --> 01:00:48,678
Noodle Dish on the Next Level.

1610
01:00:48,745 --> 01:00:50,546
Ho-young has won three times in a row,

1611
01:00:50,613 --> 01:00:52,115
and Sam has lost three times in a row.

1612
01:00:52,181 --> 01:00:54,050
Will Ho-young keep his winning streak?

1613
01:00:54,117 --> 01:00:56,919
Or will Sam break his losing streak?

1614
01:00:56,986 --> 01:00:59,956
Noodle Dish on the Next Level!

1615
01:01:00,023 --> 01:01:03,126
Who did WINTER choose?

1616
01:01:03,192 --> 01:01:04,394
-Next Level!
-Next Level!

1617
01:01:05,128 --> 01:01:05,962
Who is it?

1618
01:01:06,162 --> 01:01:07,630
SAM KIM WINS

1619
01:01:08,097 --> 01:01:09,532
SU-SU-SU-SUPER FRESH PASTA WINS

1620
01:01:09,599 --> 01:01:10,700
Sam wins.

1621
01:01:10,767 --> 01:01:13,569
THE FRESH PASTA WINS

1622
01:01:13,636 --> 01:01:15,138
That was awful, Chef Sam.

1623
01:01:15,204 --> 01:01:18,408
-Your plan worked.
-In the end, his plan worked.

1624
01:01:18,474 --> 01:01:20,009
-It did.
-It went according to plan.

1625
01:01:20,076 --> 01:01:23,746
If you rewind the tapes and check
the moment he picked up the pasta,

1626
01:01:23,813 --> 01:01:25,281
I recommended that he use it.

1627
01:01:25,748 --> 01:01:27,183
FINALLY ADMITS

1628
01:01:27,250 --> 01:01:28,184
He's scary.

1629
01:01:28,251 --> 01:01:31,320
Sam had been painting this big picture.

1630
01:01:31,387 --> 01:01:32,989
<i>How long do I cook this for?</i>

1631
01:01:33,056 --> 01:01:34,457
<i>Let me see. Give it to me.</i>

1632
01:01:34,524 --> 01:01:35,758
<i>I don't see it written anywhere.</i>

1633
01:01:35,825 --> 01:01:37,393
<i>This is the best pasta.</i>

1634
01:01:37,460 --> 01:01:40,029
<i>This is the top pasta brand.</i>

1635
01:01:40,463 --> 01:01:41,397
GETTING CHILLS…

1636
01:01:41,464 --> 01:01:42,598
I told you so.

1637
01:01:42,665 --> 01:01:44,934
Also, the heat was too weak
when he cooked the pasta.

1638
01:01:45,001 --> 01:01:47,370
-I see.
-Because pasta is cooked over high heat.

1639
01:01:47,437 --> 01:01:49,872
-You knew that?
-Why didn't you tell him?

1640
01:01:49,939 --> 01:01:52,775
-You were just watching?
-It was boiling right here.

1641
01:01:52,842 --> 01:01:55,445
-You should've told him to use high heat.
-He already knew.

1642
01:01:55,511 --> 01:01:58,748
-I thought he had a plan, so I didn't…
-That's awful!

1643
01:02:00,516 --> 01:02:02,051
What? What do you mean?

1644
01:02:02,118 --> 01:02:04,620
Sam is such a scary guy now!

1645
01:02:04,687 --> 01:02:07,123
-These stars don't mean that much.
-They don't.

1646
01:02:07,690 --> 01:02:09,058
Just let me win for once, okay?

1647
01:02:11,194 --> 01:02:12,228
SHARING HIS SORROW

1648
01:02:12,295 --> 01:02:13,529
"Let me win for once."

1649
01:02:13,596 --> 01:02:14,831
You have to understand that.

1650
01:02:14,897 --> 01:02:17,133
-Yes.
-Could've been his fourth loss in a row.

1651
01:02:17,200 --> 01:02:18,868
A four game losing streak is a bit sad.

1652
01:02:18,935 --> 01:02:20,603
You lost against him last time.

1653
01:02:20,670 --> 01:02:24,974
-Also, he's the pasta expert here.
-The game was already over.

1654
01:02:25,041 --> 01:02:27,176
Was there a particular reason?

1655
01:02:27,243 --> 01:02:30,413
The fresh noodles were so delicious

1656
01:02:30,480 --> 01:02:32,181
that the dish felt like
it was on another level,

1657
01:02:32,248 --> 01:02:34,417
-just like what I ordered.
-It was different.

1658
01:02:34,484 --> 01:02:35,985
What about the mangsu?

1659
01:02:36,052 --> 01:02:37,353
-Mangsu?
-Mangsu?

1660
01:02:37,420 --> 01:02:39,288
-Mangled <i>bingsu</i>, right?
-It's mangsu.

1661
01:02:39,355 --> 01:02:42,325
-It's still in a liquid form.
-It flooded over.

1662
01:02:42,992 --> 01:02:45,261
-It was also delicious.
-It's overflowing.

1663
01:02:45,328 --> 01:02:49,999
Does this mean Sam is now the new teacher?

1664
01:02:50,066 --> 01:02:50,900
Huh?

1665
01:02:51,300 --> 01:02:52,235
WHICH TEACHER CAPTURED YOU?

1666
01:02:52,301 --> 01:02:55,104
-Is Sung-jun gone?
-Not yet.

1667
01:02:55,171 --> 01:02:58,074
I'll decide after I try his dish later.

1668
01:02:58,141 --> 01:02:59,308
WINTER IS SLOWLY SHAKEN

1669
01:02:59,375 --> 01:03:01,010
Let me dare to say that.

1670
01:03:01,077 --> 01:03:03,746
She'll decide after tasting his food.

1671
01:03:03,813 --> 01:03:07,049
Please put a star on Sam's chest.

1672
01:03:08,284 --> 01:03:11,420
This is his seventh win!

1673
01:03:11,487 --> 01:03:12,789
-Congratulations.
-Right here.

1674
01:03:12,855 --> 01:03:15,224
-Put it above his name tag.
-Thank you for the food.

1675
01:03:15,291 --> 01:03:17,293
And the tableware.

1676
01:03:17,360 --> 01:03:20,096
Please take the tableware set.

1677
01:03:20,163 --> 01:03:21,230
It looks so cool.

1678
01:03:21,297 --> 01:03:23,499
Now, put that down and dance with her.

1679
01:03:23,566 --> 01:03:26,202
Dance with WINTER. One, two, three, four.

1680
01:03:26,269 --> 01:03:28,971
<i>Su-Su-Su-Super Fresh Pasta</i>

1681
01:03:29,038 --> 01:03:30,907
Congratulations!

1682
01:03:30,973 --> 01:03:32,208
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

1683
01:03:32,642 --> 01:03:34,410
SU-SU-SU-SUPER…

1684
01:03:34,477 --> 01:03:38,047
<i>The second cook-off</i>
<i>with ingredients from WINTER's fridge.</i>

1685
01:03:38,114 --> 01:03:42,118
Witch With a Wok, aka Yi Moon-jung,
who has been disciplining the show,

1686
01:03:42,185 --> 01:03:44,320
versus Chef Kwon Sung-jun,

1687
01:03:44,387 --> 01:03:46,989
who'll beg WINTER if he must
to escape this crisis.

1688
01:03:47,056 --> 01:03:49,625
IRON TASTE TO THE MAX LEVEL

1689
01:03:49,692 --> 01:03:53,162
Ever since Moon-jung
made her first appearance on the show,

1690
01:03:53,229 --> 01:03:55,498
